    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/associate-registrar-for-records-student-services-st-paul-minnesota-12606": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services",
      "description": "Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services in St. Paul, Minnesota | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services Bethel University St. Paul, Minnesota Share Save Job Apply for This Job Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services About the role Our Registrar's Office plays an important role in creating a student experience that is organized, responsive, and supportive from registration through graduation. As the Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services, you'll bring people together, solve complex problems, and make systems work better. You'll lead a talented student services team, helping create a culture where students, faculty, and staff receive gracious, efficient, and knowledgeable service. You'll also partner closely with colleagues across the University to coordinate registration, academic records, policies, and other processes that directly impact students. A significant part of your work will involve overseeing the traditional undergraduate registration process and the systems that support it. Your attention to detail and ability to anticipate challenges will be essential as you navigate a process with many moving pieces and stakeholders. Beyond registration, you'll have the opportunity to contribute to important academic and operational decisions. At Bethel, we believe administrative work can be deeply meaningful when it serves students and advances our mission. You'll be part of a Christ-centered community where your leadership, expertise, and commitment to excellent service can make a tangible difference in the lives of students and in the work of the University. If you're an experienced registrar professional who enjoys leading people, strengthening processes, and partnering across a university to help students thrive, we invite you to join us. This is an in-person position located in Arden Hills, MN. The starting salary range for this role is $56,900 to $61,900 annually, based on experience. What you'll do 1. Student Services Team Leadership & Collaborative Oversight - 30% - Leads the registrar student services team to work collaboratively across the university to provide gracious, efficient and effective student services. - Oversees and schedules staff for two office locations: Main Office &Mini Office/Student Services Hub. - Supervises and sets direction for team projects, processes and systems. - Serves as a collaborative partner on the University Registrar's leadership team. 2. Registration Process, SIS Configuration & Attendance Tracking Oversight - 30% - Manages the registration process, including registration window & wait lists) for the traditional undergraduate students. - Works collaboratively with University partners including faculty, staff, and students. - Responsible for configuration of the registration setup in the student information system. - Responsible for communications associated with registration, including email, e-announcements, and dept. website, for traditional undergraduate students. 3. Registrar Office Operational Support & Reporting - 40% - Manages end-of-term academic standing process and grade changes for traditional undergraduate programs and manages academic progress, dismissals, and appeals. - Maintains a working knowledge of academic policies, procedures, and curriculum and serves on various committees. - Works with the University Registrar on policy recommendations. - Collaborates with other offices on University's MOUs/Articulation Agreements. - Oversees the student filing system and record maintenance. - Provide reports that relate to registrar services. - Serve on committees, as needed. - Serve as back-up to Associate Registrar for Operations and the University Registrar. Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor's degree. Required Experience: 3+ years of progressively responsible experience in a registrar's office or similar academic administrative situation. Preferred Experience: 5+ years of progressively responsible experience in a registrar's office or similar academic administrative situation. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities - Strong knowledge of student academic records and higher education processes, including registration, degree progression, academic policies, and records management. Familiarity with the liberal arts and undergraduate education is preferred. - Proficiency with student information systems and Microsoft Office Suite; experience with Banner or a comparable higher education system is preferred. - Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy, with the ability to analyze records, identify discrepancies, interpret policies, and ensure the integrity of academic information. - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to evaluate complex situations, research applicable policies, exercise sound judgment, and develop appropriate solutions. - Excellent oral and written communication skills, with the ability to clearly explain academic policies and procedures to students, faculty, staff, and administrators. - Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work collaboratively and effectively with individuals across all levels of the University, including faculty and academic leadership. - Ability to lead, supervise, develop, and support staff, including setting clear expectations, providing feedback, and fostering a collaborative and service-oriented team environment. - Highly organized and adaptable, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and adjust effectively to changing needs and competing demands. - Proactive and self-directed, with the ability to anticipate needs, identify opportunities for process improvement, and work independently while keeping appropriate stakeholders informed. - Ability to navigate ambiguity and complexity, using sound judgment and initiative when policies, processes, or circumstances require interpretation or further investigation. - Strong commitment to customer service, with the ability to balance responsiveness and service with the consistent application of academic policies and institutional standards. - Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion and professionalism, with a strong understanding of FERPA and the appropriate handling of student educational records. Additional Responsibilities: Bethel's mission is to educate and equip students to lead lives of impact through transformative academics in a Christ-centered community. Bethel's employee community plays a central role in developing our students as whole and holy persons. To carry out this mission, Bethel uses the foundation of our guiding documents, the Affirmation of Faith, Community Covenant, and Key Policies. Bethel expects all employees to actively participate in creating our Christ-centered community by agreeing with and abiding by our core beliefs in the Affirmation of Faith and supporting all other beliefs as Biblical, responsible, and thoughtful approaches while avoiding dissension and divisiveness. Employees teach and mentor students and help one another uphold our Community Covenant commitments. As a result of these expectations, all University employees act as ministers of the gospel of Jesus Christ by actively partnering with the University to carry out its mission and foster Bethel's Christ-centered covenant community. Other Duties: The essential functions, tasks and responsibilities of this position may change from time to time. Bethel University reserves the right to add or omit duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the University or its leadership. Additional tasks or duties required of the position, will be communicated to the incumbent with specificity to ensure the employee may perform their role with complete understanding. This job description is intended to describe the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. Sponsorship Restrictions: Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Travel: This position does not require travel. Work Environment: This job operates in a professional office environment. This role routinely uses standard office equipment such as desktop and/or laptop computers, photocopiers and smartphones. The work environment involves working for a suburban, Christian university in which all employees are expected to have a demonstrated commitment and personal relationship with Jesus Christ, a commitment to the mission and values of the University, and an agreement to abide by all University policies. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk and hear. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision and ability to adjust focus. The job requires extended periods of sitting and traversing the Bethel Campus on a regular basis. Reasonable accommodations may be made to ensure people are able to perform the essential functions. The mental and physical requirements described here are representative of those that must be met by an individual to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Expected Hours of Work: Typically, days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, with the expectation to work specific schedules and hours as identified and communicated by management. Evening and weekend work may be required as job duties demand. This is a 40 hour per week, 12 months per year position. Benefits Bethel is committed to offering meaningful benefits to our employees including health insurance, retirement plans, and a generous time off package. Learn more about these offerings https://www.bethel.edu/employment/working/benefits https://www.bethel.edu/employment/working/commitment-diversity-in-hiring Applicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time Bethel University is a leader in Christ-centered higher education with approximately 4,700 students from 50 states and 32 countries enrolled in undergraduate, graduate, seminary, and adult education programs. Based in St. Paul, Minnesota, Bethel offers bachelor's and advanced degrees in nearly 100 fields. Educationally excellent classroom-based and online programs equip graduates to make exceptional contributions in life-long service to God and the world. Bethel University's Christ-centered mission includes a commitment to equal educational opportunity and equal employment opportunity. Bethel does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, national origin, sex, marital status, disability, status with regard to public assistance, familial status, or age in its admissions, educational programs, or employment practices. To apply, visit https://apptrkr.com/9798062 je-90e61ed45dc64a65b1461c907f43b192 Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Student Affairs/ Student services Related Jobs Director of Human Resources MidAmerica Nazarene University Olathe, Kansas Posted - August 28, 2026 View Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing Warner Pacific University Portland, Oregon Posted - August 27, 2026 View Vice President Academic and Dean Booth University College Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada Posted - August 12, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Portland, Oregon Oregon West Palm Beach, Florida Minnesota Iowa St. Paul, Minnesota Cedarville, Ohio Virginia Beach, Virginia Azusa, California Longview, Texas California Texas Alabama Houston, Texas ORANGE CITY, Iowa Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Virginia Florida Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Samford University Northwestern College Cedarville University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
