    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/vice-president-academic-and-dean-winnipeg-manitoba-12552": {
      "title": "Vice President Academic and Dean in Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada",
      "description": "Vice President Academic and Dean in Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Vice President Academic and Dean Booth University College Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 290 Vaughan St, Winnipeg, MB R3B 2N8, Canada The Vice President Academic and Dean is the Chief Academic Officer of the institution and is a senior member of the leadership team . The Vice President Academic and Dean works together with the President and the University College Cabinet to implement the strategic goals of Booth University College. The Vice President Academic and Dean leads, directs, and manages the academic programs of the institution and must be able to work strategically, tactically, and operationally . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: Supervises all academic departments and directly supervises Dean, School for Continuing Studies and any other academic deans, Director of Library Services, Registrar, Faculty (may be delegated to a dean), Administrative Coordinator, and Coordinator, Field Education and Work Placement Programs ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB/ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Lead the development, implementation, and evaluation of Booth's academic strategic priorities, ensuring alignment with Booth’s Strategic Plan Provide leadership for institutional accreditation, quality assurance, academic assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives Serve as a liaison between academic staff and administrative leadership Oversee assessment of student learning outcomes, program effectiveness, and institutional academic performance\\ Work closely with School Directors, Faculty, Student Services, and Students on issues of academic integrity, academic probation, and student accessibility Promote scholarship, research, and faculty professional development consistent with Booth's mission Foster excellence in teaching through faculty mentoring, professional development, performance management, and succession planning Provide leadership for new programs and curriculum development, and for innovation in teaching and learning technologies Participate in institutional planning including enrollment, budgeting, risk management, and long-term organizational sustainability Champion academic excellence, student success, retention, and graduation outcomes. Foster a collaborative, respectful, and mission-centered academic culture characterized by integrity, collegiality, and servant leadership Provide leadership and direction for academic affairs by setting goals and monitoring and ensuring implementation Strengthen the distinctive missional identity of Booth University College by ensuring programs, course curriculum, and other academic events align to the purpose and mission of Booth UC Provide oversight on all academic appointments, tenure, and promotions, and ensure that processes comply with the Faculty Manual and other University College policies Provide oversight, vision, and strategic direction in academic budgeting and staff planning. In collaboration with the Dean of SCS, oversee the academic relationship with The Salvation Army College for Officer Training Schedule and oversee academic program reviews and work with Deans and School Directors to study and develop reviews, improvement processes, and/or changes to academic policies. Work with the President to strengthen relationships with The Salvation Army, accreditation bodies, external organizations, and other academic institutions Represent the President in select forums as required Serve as Vice Chair of Senate and the Senate Planning & Priorities Committee. Perform other duties as assigned by the PresidentDevelop and maintain strong, positive relationships within The Salvation Army, both in the Canada and Bermuda Territory and internationally QUALIFICATIONS 1. Required PhD or other terminal degree 7 years of senior or executive leadership experience A scholar with a proven record of teaching and research Experienced manager with organizational abilities, financial acumen, proficient in change management and conflict resolution Fully supportive of the integration of faith and learning in a Christian university-level setting and a commitment to the Mission of Booth University College Strong understanding of higher education in Canada (both public and private) with knowledge of the Manitoba higher education landscape Must have exceptional communication skills Must have the ability for strategic thinking Experience in governance and policy development Working knowledge of the church in Canada, including The Salvation Army. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain networks and partnerships to facilitate goal accomplishments Satisfactory criminal record check Must be legally entitled to work in Canada 2. Assets (Preferred Qualifications) Working knowledge of various technologies (including AI), especially as they relate to higher education A Salvationist in good standing This is a full-time position with 37.5 hours per week. Booth University College offers a stimulating university college environment, a mission-driven purpose, and the opportunity to contribute to change as Booth UC moves forward on its commitment to its mission: Education for a Better World. How to Apply: Application materials should include the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of faith and how your faith commitment would contribute to fulfilling the mission of Booth UC Names and contact information for three references Applications and requests for further information may be submitted in confidence to the Human Resources Generalist; Booth University College by email: ( BoothUC.Careers@boothuc.ca ). Applications will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. Accommodations are available upon request throughout the recruitment process. About Booth University College Booth UC is a Christian university college located in Winnipeg, Manitoba (Canada) and rooted in The Salvation Army’s history of meeting the needs of the most vulnerable in society. As an open-enrollment institution, we welcome students from many different backgrounds, cultures, and countries. Deeply committed to social justice, we blend Christian faith and rigorous scholarship with a passion for service. Our approach to learning is anchored in academic excellence and based on a vision of social justice, hope, and mercy for all. We are committed to our mission: Education for a Better World. This is described in our mission statement: William and Catherine Booth University College, a Christian university college rooted in The Salvation Army’s Wesleyan theological tradition, brings together Christian faith, rigorous scholarship, and a passion for service. The University College educates students to understand the complexities of our world, to develop the knowledge and skills necessary to be active contributors to society, and to know how the Christian faith compels them to bring hope, social justice, and mercy into our world. Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Chief Executives/ Executive Directors Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services Bethel University St. Paul, Minnesota Posted - September 1, 2026 View Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing Warner Pacific University Portland, Oregon Posted - August 27, 2026 View Major Gifts Officer Arizona Christian University Glendale, Arizona Posted - August 18, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Texas Houston, Texas Birmingham, Alabama California Florida Alabama Charleston, South Carolina Virginia Beach, Virginia Virginia Longview, Texas South Carolina ORANGE CITY, Iowa Cedarville, Ohio Grand Rapids, Michigan Azusa, California Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Ohio Michigan Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Palm Beach Atlantic University Calvin University Samford University Regent University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Northwestern College Charleston Southern University Cedarville University Trending Categories Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Religion Executive Faculty Careers - Engineering Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713 Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-of-finance-9-mo-tt-birmingham-alabama-12524": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance (9 Mo, TT)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Finance (9 Mo, TT) in Birmingham, Alabama | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor of Finance (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Share Save Job Apply for This Job Assistant Professor of Finance (9-month, Tenure Track) July 28, 2026 Samford University’s Brock School of Business invites individuals interested in serving in a Christian university environment to apply for an Assistant Professor of Finance faculty position within the Economics, Finance & Quantitative Analysis Department. This tenure track faculty position is a nine-month appointment beginning in August 2027 . Applicants for this position must exhibit strong teaching skills, be committed to maintaining an ongoing research effort, and work effectively and collegially with faculty, students and colleagues. The normal teaching load for faculty is 3 courses per semester, and research is required, commensurate with the teaching load. Summer teaching and competitive research grants are also available. Qualified candidates will hold an earned doctorate from an AACSB and institutionally accredited university in Finance and preferably with teaching experience/interests in a variety of finance courses. ABDs near completion will be considered and hired at the rank of Instructor with commensurate salary. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated skills, abilities, or experience in teaching. In the fall of 2015, Brock School of Business moved into a 75,000-square-foot, state-of-the-art building that provides excellent space for faculty to interact with students, colleagues and the regional business community. Brock School of Business is accredited by AACSB International, and hosts more than 1,000 students in its undergraduate, M.Acc. and M.B.A. programs. For more information, please go to samford.edu/business . Located in the Homewood suburb of Birmingham, Alabama, Samford ( samford.edu ) is a leading Christian university offering undergraduate programs grounded in the liberal arts with an array of nationally recognized graduate and professional schools. Founded in 1841, Samford enrolls 6,324 students from 44 states, Puerto Rico and 16 countries in its 10 academic schools with 450 full-time faculty. Samford is ranked #3 in the nation for career preparation and #7 in the nation for student learning opportunities as listed in The Wall Street Journal (2026). The University is dedicated to the promotion of rigorous academic inquiry in a Christian setting. The University seeks and prefers employee applicants of the Christian faith and offers competitive salaries with a generous benefits package. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until October 15, 2026. Teaching duties begin in August 2027. Application materials should include a cover letter outlining teaching and professional interests and expertise, curriculum vitae, application for faculty position (link below), faculty applicant Christian Mission Statement (link below) and a list of three professional references with contact information. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States, as Samford will not sponsor any employment visas for this position. Salary is dependent upon qualifications and experience. The successful candidate must pass a background check. “Application for Faculty Position” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/Human_Resources/application-for-faculty-employment.pdf “Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/academic-affairs/Faculty-Applicant-Christian-Mission-Statement.docx Please submit all materials in PDF format to: [email protected] Subject: Assistant Professor of Finance For questions about the position contact: Dr. Rusty Yerkes, Search Committee Chair [email protected] or 205/726-2051 In accordance with applicable federal and state laws, such as Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act and ADA Amendments, the University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, color, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, religion, or any other protected status under federal, state or local law applicable to the University, in its education policies, programs, and activities, in its admissions policies, in employment policies and practices, and all other areas of the University. As a faith-based institution, the University is exempted from certain laws and regulations concerning discrimination. Job Information Job Category: Accounting / Finance Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Business-Economics Faculty Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - April 29, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Cybersecurity Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Spring Arbor University Spring Arbor, Michigan Posted - September 8, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations South Carolina Houston, Texas Grand Rapids, Michigan Charleston, South Carolina Ohio Longview, Texas Cedarville, Ohio Michigan Iowa Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Virginia Virginia Beach, Virginia California Texas Azusa, California West Palm Beach, Florida Birmingham, Alabama Florida Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Samford University Charleston Southern University Houston Christian University Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University Calvin University Northwestern College LeTourneau University Trending Categories Executive Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Psychology Education Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/provost-and-executive-vice-president-clinton-mississippi-12629": {
      "title": "Provost and Executive Vice President in Clinton, Mississippi",
      "description": "Provost and Executive Vice President in Clinton, Mississippi | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Share Save Job Apply for This Job Mississippi Christian University invites applicants for the position of Provost and Executive Vice President. The University’s No. 2 leadership position encompasses broad responsibilities and duties to oversee the institution’s academic mission. On June 1, 2026, the institution’s name was changed from Mississippi College to Mississippi Christian University, while also retaining the shortened “MC.” The institution's new name reflects its Mississippi roots, Christian mission, and university status. Founded in 1826, MC is the oldest institution of higher learning in Mississippi. Affiliated with the Mississippi Baptist Convention, MC is a comprehensive Christian university recognized for academic excellence and commitment to the cause of Christ. Offering undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs, the University prepares students to lead lives of purpose and service. For the second year in a row, the Wall Street Journal/College Pulse named MC to its list of 2026 Best Colleges in the U.S., and in fall 2026,  MC was the highest-ranked private university in Mississippi in U.S. News & World Report ’s list of Best National Universities. The University was also named to the 2025 and 2026 Phi Theta Kappa Honor Society’s Transfer Honor Roll. MC is also in the top 8% of Christian Colleges in America and the No. 1 college in Mississippi for Academics (Niche, 2026). Mississippi Christian University enrolls approximately 4,000 students from 41 states and 40 countries. Graduate and professional schools include the MC School of Law in Jackson, the state’s first master’s degree in physician assistant studies, and more than 60 other exemplary graduate programs. The University continually seeks the highest academic standards, and many programs are accredited by external independent accrediting organizations. MC is in good standing with its regional accreditor and has been since its initial accreditation in 1922.  Schools comprising the core of MC include Business; Christian Studies, Humanities, and the Arts; Education and Human Sciences; Law; Nursing; and Science and Mathematics. Throughout 2026, MC is celebrating its bicentennial, looking back over 200 years of connecting faith and education, and looking forward to a new century of empowering students to impact the world. MC is the first institution of higher learning in Mississippi to reach a 200 year anniversary. The University’s global outreach includes a wide range of study abroad opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate students. MC’s endowment exceeds $105 million, and the University employs more than 500 people. MC is located in Clinton, which is 15 miles west of Jackson, the state’s capital. With an A+ rating, Clinton Public Schools are consistently ranked among Mississippi’s top-rated public school districts. Designated as a Mississippi Main Street City, a Mississippi Most Livable City, and a Certified Retirement City, Clinton is a family-friendly city with events and activities to encourage positive community experiences and relationships. The links below provide more information about our University. Mission and Vision: https://www.mc.edu/about/mission Academic Accolades: https://www.mc.edu/admissions/why-mc National and Regional Rankings: https://www.mc.edu/about/rankings Quick Facts: https://www.mc.edu/institutional-research/quick-facts City of Clinton Information: https://www.clintonms.org/about Duties of the position : The Provost and Executive Vice President works closely with the President and the President’s Council consisting of deans, vice presidents and other key administrators. The University’s chief academic executive brings vision, energy, and commitment to the advancement of programs at undergraduate and graduate levels and works closely with Academic Deans over all six schools. The current Organizational Chart notes the direct reports, although the exact structure may vary based on the skill set of the incoming Provost and Executive Vice President. The executive will focus on pursuing the institution’s vision to achieve academic excellence with a commitment to the cause of Christ. Strengthening the faculty, knowledge of challenges facing American higher education, and strategies to enhance the institution’s national reputation are all paramount to the position at Mississippi Christian University. The Provost and Executive Vice President leads and serves as the institution’s second in command. The academic leader will guide the institution with administrative skills, creativity, expertise, and coordination as the University builds its core mission. Emphasizing the personal, professional, and intellectual growth of the faculty, staff, and students are all essential to shaping Mississippi Christian University for decades to come. The Provost has the opportunity and responsibility to care for students and help them maximize their potential in a higher education setting. Qualifications: Ph.D./terminal degree Proven experience in academic leadership Successful leadership skills A demonstrated commitment to the Christian faith Exemplary communication skills A proven track record in team building skills Commitment to the vision and mission of Mississippi Christian University Creative approaches to changing aspects of higher education in the 21st Century Confidential inquiries, nominations, referrals, applicant questions, and applicant materials should be directed to Dr. Stephanie Busbea at the address below. To apply for this position, submit a letter of interest, including answers to the following questions, and a detailed vitae/resume. Describe your Christian faith commitment. Share details about your faith journey, involvement with your local church, and participation in any faith-related organizations or ministries. Discuss your philosophy of Christian higher education and how it relates to the intellectual, spiritual, and social formation of students. How do you define and cultivate academic excellence at a private, non-profit, Christian University amidst the changing landscape of higher education in the 21st century? Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  The search will remain confidential until the finalist(s) are invited to campus. Dr. Stephanie Busbea Mississippi Christian University Interim Provost Chair, Provost Search Advisory Committee MC Box 4002, Clinton, MS 39058 sdb@mc.edu (601) 925-3202 Mississippi Christian University uses Dynamic Forms for the employment application process. To apply, you must create an account with Dynamic Forms. Once logged in, select the Staff application type You will be required to upload a cover letter and resume Job Information Job Category: Executive Related Jobs Payroll and Benefits Manager Asbury University Wilmore, Kentucky Posted - September 10, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Biology Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View Instructor of Mathematics Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science Belhaven University Jackson, Mississippi Posted - September 10, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations South Carolina Michigan Alabama Azusa, California Iowa Charleston, South Carolina Ohio Florida Cedarville, Ohio Grand Rapids, Michigan Virginia Houston, Texas Birmingham, Alabama California West Palm Beach, Florida Longview, Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia ORANGE CITY, Iowa Texas Trending Companies Houston Christian University Northwestern College Charleston Southern University Calvin University Samford University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Cedarville University Trending Categories Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Health Professions Executive Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Apply for this job Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More… Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/payroll-and-benefits-manager-wilmore-kentucky-12628": {
      "title": "Payroll and Benefits Manager in Wilmore, Kentucky",
      "description": "Payroll and Benefits Manager in Wilmore, Kentucky | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Payroll and Benefits Manager Asbury University Wilmore, Kentucky Share Save Job Apply for This Job Reports to : Assoc. VP of Human Resources, Risk Management, and Project Manager FLSA Classification: E xempt Job Purpose : The Benefits and Payroll Manager is a key member of the Human Resources team and assists in all areas of Human Resources. The position has primary responsibility for the daily administration of all employee benefits plans and payroll. Meets with employees to discuss and resolve any benefit questions or issues that arise. Oversees the distribution of all relevant compensation materials and ensures that all requests for payment are made in a timely manner and fall within budgetary limits. An important part of the position is supporting the ministry and mission of the University and advancing the academic excellence and spiritual vitality of our University and students. Each employee plays an important role in the development of the Christian faith in our students. Essential Functions: Benefits Administration Administration of all employee benefits plans including meeting with new benefit eligible employees. Coordinates on boarding of all benefit eligible employees. Develops communication pieces (including print, electronic, and web) for annual open enrollment and ongoing benefit information. Maintains all benefit enrollment and termination records and ensures compliance with all applicable benefit regulations and laws. Coordinates annual benefit open enrollment. Manages the resolution of claims and billing issues. Reviews and recommends implementation of renewal and new benefit contracts. Oversees the tuition waiver program and graduate loan program and tracks data on program usage. Oversees the enrollment and education processes of the retirement plan. Coordinates all appropriate exit materials, performs exit interviews for all exiting employees, and tracks responses to exit survey materials. Manages and coordinates annual retirement plan audit. Payroll Administration Works directly with Assoc VP regarding all aspects of university payroll, including time and attendance, payroll processing, tax withholding and submittal, and implementation of University payroll policy. Updates the Payroll system for regular employee data and works to maintains accurate records of employee compensation and other matters. Compensation Works with various campus offices and departments to ensure timely and accurate processing of payment requests. Workers Compensation Works directly with the insurance carrier and employee for all workers compensation claims. Maintains OSHA 300 log and files annual report. General HR duties Maintains all employee files both paper and electronic, assists with the development and updating of policies for the Employee Handbook. Works with the AVP to oversee the performance management process including preparation and distribution of evaluations, receiving completed forms, scoring, and statistical tracking of performance data. Works directly with the AVP for the management of all special events overseen by the HR Office. This includes employee Christmas celebration, new employee orientation, retirement/farewell receptions and other trainings/programs. Issues all FML notices and tracks FML time for applicable employees as well as meets with employees and supervisors to educate them on FML. Supervises student workers in the office. May assist the AVP in conducting employee relations meetings. Oversees the employee recognition program including tracking years of service as well as ordering awards and preparation of certificates. In the absence of the AVP may assist in supervision of the HR Assistant. Regularly updates the AVP of Human Resources and Risk Management on all matters related to the operations of the HR office. Assists the AVP with legal matters or other projects, as determined by the AVP. Other duties as assigned. Physical Requirements: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. This position requires the ability to occasionally lift office products and supplies, up to 20 pounds. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work : This is a full-time on-site position, and hours of work and days are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Travel: No travel is expected for this position. Qualifications : A bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university (candidates with over ten years of benefits or human resources experience may substitute experience for a degree). 3-5 years of previous benefits administration and/or human resources experience. A high degree of proficiency with word processing and spreadsheet functions. Excellent customer service skills. An ability to appropriately work with highly confidential material. Excellent technological, verbal and written communication skills. Human resources certification is preferred (PHR, SHRM-CP). A committed and dynamic Christian faith is vital along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards and mission. Other Duties : Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Institutional Commitment: Asbury University is an independent, Christian, liberal arts university in the Wesleyan-Holiness tradition. In the desire to be a more inclusive community, reflective of the Kingdom of God, we especially encourage applications from women and from candidates from various ethnic backgrounds. At Asbury University, employees must display a committed and dynamic Christian faith along with the ability to support the University’s theological position, lifestyle standards, and mission. Candidates must agree, support and adhere to University policies and procedures – including the Faculty Manual, Community Standards Guidelines, Human Sexuality Statement, and the Standard of Conduct for employees. Asbury University does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, or handicap in its educational programs, activities, or employment practices. < Job Information Job Category: Human Resources Education: Bachelor's Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Related Jobs Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology or Kinesiology Simpson University Redding, California Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Part Time Doctoral Faculty - Artificial Intelligence Anderson University - SC Remote Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Cedarville, Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Grand Rapids, Michigan Charleston, South Carolina California South Carolina Longview, Texas Virginia Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Houston, Texas Iowa Florida Virginia Beach, Virginia Michigan Azusa, California Texas Trending Companies Calvin University Cedarville University Regent University Charleston Southern University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Azusa Pacific University Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University Northwestern College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Executive Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More… Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
