    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/faculty-position-in-department-of-sports-medicine-exercise-science-jackson-mississippi-12627": {
      "title": "FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science",
      "description": "FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science in Jackson, Mississippi | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science Belhaven University Jackson, Mississippi Share Save Job Apply for This Job Belhaven University is seeking a faculty member in Sports Medicine & Exercise Science. The position is open-rank and tenure-track. The Sports Medicine & Exercise Science curriculum integrates basic and applied sciences to prepare students for a wide range of careers in the healthcare and wellness industries. The bachelor’s degree prepares students for graduate/professional programs and careers in fulfilling vocations such as physical and occupational therapy, athletic training, chiropractic medicine, exercise physiology, strength and conditioning, and personal training. Belhaven University is an innovative and academically progressive institution built on the timeless principles of scholarship, service, and Biblical truth. “Our Standard is Christ” is the Belhaven identifier because, as an institution, we are committed to honoring the Lord in all we do. Responsibilities Candidate responsibilities will include: · Teaching undergraduate Sports Medicine & Exercise Science courses, which may include Kinesiology, Medical Terminology, Injury Care & Prevention, Exercise Testing & Prescription, Biomechanics, Sport & Exercise Nutrition, Exercise Physiology, Physiology & Psychology of Movement, and Professional Development. · Supervising student clinical observational/shadowing experiences · Serving as an advisor and mentor regarding students' academic plans and career paths. · Serving as an advisor to the student pre-professional club. While not required, candidates will be encouraged to conduct externally funded research and/or other scholarly activities, such as journal publications, conference presentations, etc. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Human Performance, or related discipline is required. Applicants must be able to articulate a Christian worldview in one’s teaching and academic discipline and fully support the University vision, mission and statement of faith . The candidate should contribute to the spiritual and academic fellowship of the University. How to Apply A confidential review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please submit the following: · A CV and a cover letter outlining your suitability for this position, including an explanation of your interest in Christian higher education · A 3 to 4 paragraph statement of how you would integrate the Biblical worldview into your instructional content · A brief account (750 words or less) of your spiritual pilgrimage, including the time and circumstances surrounding your becoming a believer in Christ and your current relationship with Christ. R eview Belhaven University’s Commitment Statement, including our employee expectations (www.belhaven.edu). Should you receive a job offer, you will be asked to accept this agreement by signing it. Employment at Belhaven University is contingent upon the results of an independent background check. Confidential questions and formal applications may be submitted to: Monica French, Project Manager for Academic Affairs [email protected] Job Information Job Category: Education Salary: $70,000.00 - $85,000.00 Commensurate with Experience Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Payroll and Benefits Manager Asbury University Wilmore, Kentucky Posted - September 10, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Instructor of Mathematics Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Biology Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Charleston, South Carolina California Houston, Texas Michigan Virginia Beach, Virginia Grand Rapids, Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Azusa, California Longview, Texas South Carolina Birmingham, Alabama Ohio Cedarville, Ohio Iowa Florida Alabama Virginia Trending Companies Northwestern College Regent University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Cedarville University Palm Beach Atlantic University Samford University Calvin University Azusa Pacific University Charleston Southern University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Education Executive Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities