    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/english-professor-longview-texas-12624": {
      "title": "English Professor",
      "description": "English Professor in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job English Professor LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA LeTourneau University, a vibrant and growing interdenominational, evangelical Christian university, known for high-quality STEM programs that attract students of outstanding academic ability, invites applications and nominations for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor of English, Department of Humanities & Social Sciences. This is a tenure-track position, with rank negotiable based on experience. This faculty member will teach a range of composition courses. The ideal candidate should have excellent team-building skills and the interest and experience to provide growth to the Department of Humanities & Social Sciences. Research and teaching experience are highly desired. This is a nine-month position with the possibility of summer teaching. Classes and other responsibilities are conducted primarily on weekdays but could include some evening classes and independent studies.  Attendance is required at some evening and weekend events. RESPONSIBILITIES : •\tTeach a full-time load (12 credit hours per term) of courses in English composition and writing, including both lower and upper division coursework, in a highly engaging way •\tContribute to the development of writing courses in the classical rhetorical tradition •\tParticipate actively in the university learning community by serving on department, school, and/or university committees and special service assignments •\tParticipate in student advising, success, and retention programs •\tMaintain an active agenda of scholarship or professional engagement within the discipline QUALIFICATIONS : •\tLeTourneau University seeks an individual with an enthusiastic and contagious Christian faith who is committed to teaching, research, and leadership at a small, dynamic Christian University where the integration of faith and academic excellence is paramount. The candidate must be in genuine agreement with the University’s Statement of Faith and Community Covenant for life and work at LeTourneau. •\tAn earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in English, Rhetoric & Composition, from an accredited university or in a closely related field. Candidates with a Master’s in English or Rhetoric & Composition with significant experience teaching classical rhetoric and composition may be considered. •\tCommitment to working within a program emphasizing primary texts in the Great Books Tradition. Knowledge of Latin preferred •\tDemonstrated teaching competency •\tInterpersonal skills to effectively and professionally interact with students, colleagues, and administrators in a university learning community •\tThe successful candidate will be able to think creatively and critically about the essential role of the humanities (and writing, in particular) within the “Christian Polytechnic University” mission and provide leadership for efforts to fully infuse the humanities within the learning environment and campus culture of LeTourneau University. This includes developing communication and analytical skills in students majoring in technical fields such as engineering, aviation, computer science, etc. SALARY AND BENEFITS: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. DATE POSITION IS AVAILABLE: Fall 2027 PROCEDURE FOR APPLICATION OR NOMINATION: Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. The review process will begin as early as October 15th, 2026, and all applications received by October 30th, 2026, will receive full consideration. Applications after that date will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty. Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information.  Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Faculty, Clinical Psychology - College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations West Palm Beach, Florida Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Florida California Grand Rapids, Michigan Iowa Charleston, South Carolina Cedarville, Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Ohio Houston, Texas Virginia Virginia Beach, Virginia Alabama South Carolina Longview, Texas Azusa, California Texas Trending Companies Cedarville University Charleston Southern University LeTourneau University Azusa Pacific University Samford University Northwestern College Palm Beach Atlantic University Calvin University Regent University Houston Christian University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Executive Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/computer-science-faculty-grand-rapids-michigan-12623": {
      "title": "Computer Science Faculty in Grand Rapids, Michigan",
      "description": "Computer Science Faculty in Grand Rapids, Michigan | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Computer Science Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Share Save Job Apply for This Job Calvin University invites applications for a full-time regular (tenure-track) faculty member to join the Computer Science Department to teach lower- and upper-level courses in computer science beginning on July 1, 2027 (pending administrative approval). REQUIREMENTS The university seeks applicants with vibrant Christian faith who are dedicated to integration of that faith with their field of study. Ideal candidates will hold a PhD in computer science, data science, or a related field.  Candidates with a master’s degree in computer science and five years of relevant experience will also be considered. Candidates are expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level and have an active stream of relevant research and publication. Preference will be given to candidates with experience teaching using a variety of methods and instructional technology. The university will prioritize candidates with broad interdisciplinary interests, demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion, ability to integrate questions of meaning, significance, and ethics into all course content, and deep commitment to engaging students beyond the classroom. FACULTY RESPONSIBILITIES Faculty members typically teach 24 semester hours per academic year. Faculty are expected to grow in Reformed Christian commitment, to pursue an active scholarly agenda, to teach effectively, and to serve the university, department, students, and the wider community. Candidates will be asked to affirm their commitment to the educational mission of Calvin University as a Christian liberal arts university in the Reformed tradition, affiliated with the Christian Reformed Church.  (See Educating for Shalom and Faculty Expectations .) Calvin University provides numerous faculty development opportunities to foster growth in these commitments. FACULTY RESOURCES Calvin University stands at the forefront of Christian scholarship across disciplines. The university hosts a number of Centers and Institutes and provides other funding opportunities to support faculty teaching and research, including sabbaticals, grants, course releases, summer research stipends, travel funds, and student research opportunities. ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT The Department of Computer Science includes six full-time faculty and a full-time systems engineer to support classes and research in the department. Computer Science especially seeks candidates in machine learning or cybersecurity, but candidates in all fields are encouraged to apply. The department offers a minor, a Cybersecurity certificate program, and two majors, including a BCS degree accredited by ABET. Jointly with the Department of Mathematics and Statistics , it offers a major in data science which includes courses in programming, statistics, machine learning, visualization, ethics, and various electives. The department features supportive colleagues, excellent facilities, disciplined students, including many international students, support for women in STEM, and strong undergraduate majors. ABOUT CALVIN UNIVERSITY Calvin University is a top-ranked national university that equips students to think deeply, to act justly, and to live wholeheartedly as Christ’s agents of renewal in the world. Approximately 3,600 Calvin students study the liberal arts and select from a broad range of majors and professional programs, including a growing portfolio of graduate level offerings. The university is located in Grand Rapids, Michigan , in a thriving metropolitan region of approximately one million people situated equidistant from Chicago and Detroit. Furthermore, the West Michigan region is ranked by Forbes as the #1 place to raise a family. For more information, please visit http://www.calvin.edu/go/facultyopenings . Calvin is building a tradition of diversity and accessibility and welcomes applications from persons whose personal characteristics will further that commitment.  Calvin does not discriminate in the employment of individuals on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, disability, sex, or age.  Calvin University is an educational agency of the Christian Reformed Church and, in compliance with Title VII and other applicable law, reserves the right to give preference in employment based upon religion. Please note that, while we welcome applications from all qualified applicants, employment opportunities for foreign nationals may be subject to additional eligibility, timing, sponsorship, and funding considerations under current U.S. immigration and visa requirements. TO APPLY Complete the online application process and attach the following: Letter of application that addresses the requirements and responsibilities of the position, including your interest in teaching and scholarship at a Reformed Christian University Full curriculum vitae Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  Questions can be sent to Derek Schuurman, chair of the Computer Science Department, at derek.schuurman@calvin.edu with the subject heading “COMPUTER SCIENCE FACULTY OPENING”. FAITH and EDUCATIONAL COMMITMENT 1. Commitment to the educational mission of Calvin as a Christian liberal arts university affiliated with the Christian Reformed Church. 2. A commitment to the Christian faith and to the integration of faith, learning, and student development. DIVERSITY COMMITMENT Demonstrated awareness and commitment to effectively establishing relationships and positive communication across multiple dimensions of diversity including, but not limited to, race, gender, physical limitations, class, or religious perspectives. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Computer science Education: Doctorate Degree Related Jobs Computer Science Faculty Position College of the Ozarks Point Lookout, Missouri Posted - August 21, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty, Artificial Intelligence & Analytics Indiana Wesleyan University Remote Posted - July 28, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Posted - September 15, 2026 View Part Time Doctoral Faculty - Artificial Intelligence Anderson University - SC Remote Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Florida Alabama Longview, Texas Charleston, South Carolina West Palm Beach, Florida Cedarville, Ohio Grand Rapids, Michigan Iowa Texas Ohio Michigan Virginia Beach, Virginia Azusa, California ORANGE CITY, Iowa California South Carolina Houston, Texas Virginia Birmingham, Alabama Trending Companies Northwestern College Houston Christian University Charleston Southern University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Calvin University Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Cedarville University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Education Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713 Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
