    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/adjunct-faculty-college-math-for-elementary-teaching-chicago-illinois-12620": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching in Chicago, Illinois | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 820 N La Salle Dr, Chicago, IL 60610, USA Location : Onsite, Chicago, IL Employment Type: Part-Time Salary: $ 2,250 Stipend paid over 5 months Start Date: January 2027 Department: Undergraduate School Help Future Educators Build Confidence and Competence in Mathematics. Moody Bible Institute is seeking an engaging and student-focused Adjunct Faculty Member in College Math for Elementary Teaching to prepare future educators for success in both the classroom and the Illinois teacher licensure exam. We are looking for an instructor who combines strong mathematical expertise with a passion for teaching and mentoring students, helping them develop the foundational knowledge, reasoning skills, and confidence needed to succeed as future teachers. The ideal candidate is an effective communicator who can make mathematical concepts accessible, provide clear and systematic instruction, and foster a supportive learning environment that encourages student growth and achievement. About Us Moody Bible Institute is a Christ-centered higher education and media ministry dedicated to equipping people with the truth of God's Word. Through trusted biblical teaching, media, and educational resources, Moody reaches audiences around the world with the gospel and seeks to make a lasting Kingdom impact. The Opportunity The Adjunct Faculty Member will teach College Math for Elementary Teaching (ISBE), an undergraduate course designed to strengthen students' mathematical understanding and prepare them for the professional content knowledge required for teacher licensure. The instructor will provide engaging classroom instruction, assess student learning, and support students as they develop the mathematical reasoning and problem-solving skills necessary for future success as educators. What You’ll Do Provide high-quality instruction for undergraduate students enrolled in College Math for Elementary Teaching. Develop and deliver engaging lessons that promote mathematical understanding and problem-solving skills. Assess student learning through assignments, examinations, and other evaluation methods. Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. Foster a positive and encouraging learning environment that supports student success. Maintain accurate course records, grades, and documentation. Adhere to institutional policies, academic standards, and course outcomes. Communicate effectively with students and academic leadership. Perform other instructional duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in      Mathematics, Accounting, Education, or a related field. Master's degree from      an accredited institution. Strong knowledge of      college-level mathematics concepts and applications. Ability to effectively      communicate mathematical concepts to diverse learners. Commitment to student      success, academic excellence, and Christian higher education. Alignment with Moody      Bible Institute's Doctrinal Statement. Preferred Teaching experience in      mathematics at the high school or college level. Experience preparing      students for standardized assessments or teacher licensure examinations. Demonstrated ability      to motivate and support students with varying levels of mathematical      preparedness. Experience using      effective instructional and assessment strategies that support student      achievement. Work Environment This is a part-time adjunct faculty position located on Moody Bible Institute's Chicago campus. In-person instruction is required. Classes meet two days per week for 1 hour and 15      minutes per class session. Appointment is anticipated for the Spring 2027      semester (January through May, 16 weeks). Additional Information Candidates must demonstrate alignment with Moody      Bible Institute's mission, doctrinal beliefs, and Christian values. Employees are required to affirm Moody's Statement of      Faith and adhere to Community Standards. Moody Bible Institute values diversity and seeks team      members who engage others in ways that honor its biblical foundation. Moody complies with applicable nondiscrimination laws      and, as a religious institution, requires employees to hold beliefs      consistent with its Doctrinal Statement and Community Standards. Why Join Us? At Moody, education is more than a career. It is a calling to invest in the next generation of Christian leaders. As a faculty member, you will have the opportunity to mentor students, shape future ministry practitioners, and contribute to a Christ-centered learning community committed to biblical truth and ministry excellence. In addition to meaningful work, eligible employees enjoy a comprehensive benefits package that may include: Retirement benefits with institutional contributions Free membership to the Solheim Athletic Center Free On-Campus Parking A collaborative and mission-driven academic community The opportunity to influence the next generation of      Christian leaders Join us and help prepare the next generation of educators through exceptional teaching, meaningful mentorship, and a commitment to Christ-centered learning. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Mathematics Education: Master's Degree Experience: Less than 2 years Related Jobs Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Michigan Birmingham, Alabama Virginia Azusa, California Ohio Iowa Florida Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia Charleston, South Carolina Alabama Cedarville, Ohio Grand Rapids, Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Longview, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida South Carolina Houston, Texas California Trending Companies Regent University Samford University LeTourneau University Charleston Southern University Azusa Pacific University Northwestern College Houston Christian University Cedarville University Palm Beach Atlantic University Calvin University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Education Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Executive Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
