    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-of-children-and-family-ministry-chicago-illinois-12619": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry in Chicago, Illinois | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location N LaSalle St, Chicago, IL, USA Location : Onsite, Chicago, IL Employment Type: Full-Time Compensation Minimum Annual Salary: $ 60,000 - 70,000 Start Date: January 2027 Department: Applied Theology and Church Ministries The compensation above is the estimated hiring for this position. Rank and salary are commensurate with academic credentials and experience. Final offers are determined based on a variety of factors including skills, experience, qualifications, internal equity, and other job-related considerations. Equip the Next Generation. Strengthen Families. Advance the Gospel. Moody Bible Institute invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry to join the Applied Theology and Church Ministries Department at our Chicago campus. We are seeking a dedicated scholar, experienced ministry practitioner, and gifted educator who is passionate about preparing students to serve children, parents, and families through biblically grounded and ministry-focused leadership. This position offers an exciting opportunity to shape future ministry leaders while contributing to the growth and impact of Moody's Children and Family Ministry program. The ideal candidate will bring a combination of academic excellence, practical ministry experience, and entrepreneurial initiative to support program development, student engagement, ministry partnerships, and curriculum innovation. About Us Moody Bible Institute is a Christ-centered higher education and media ministry dedicated to equipping people with the truth of God's Word. Through trusted biblical teaching, media, and educational resources, Moody reaches audiences around the world with the gospel and seeks to make a lasting Kingdom impact. The Opportunity The Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry serves as a faculty member within the Undergraduate School and provides academic leadership as Program Head for the Children and Family Ministry major. This role is responsible for teaching, mentoring students, overseeing internships and ministry experiences, and contributing to the strategic development of the program. The successful candidate will help advance Moody Bible Institute's mission of providing a Bible-centered education that equips students to know Christ and make Him known through effective ministry in churches, organizations, families, and communities around the world. What You’ll Do Teach undergraduate courses in Children and Family      Ministry, including biblical foundations, applied theology, child      discipleship, family ministry, and practical ministry leadership. Develop course syllabi, learning outcomes, and      assessments that support academic excellence and ministry preparation. Serve as Program Head for the Children and Family      Ministry major, providing program leadership, oversight, and strategic      direction. Design, coordinate, and oversee internships,      service-learning experiences, and community engagement opportunities. Teach in multiple instructional formats, including      in-person and online learning environments. Advise and mentor students in their academic,      vocational, and spiritual development. Maintain regular office hours and an active campus      presence. Collaborate with faculty and institutional leaders to      support program growth, ministry partnerships, curriculum development, and      scholarly engagement. Participate in faculty meetings, committee      responsibilities, and institutional initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Master's degree in Children's Ministry, Applied      Theology, Christian Education, Ministry Leadership, or a related field. Ability to teach across related disciplines,      including Applied Theology, Church Ministries, Elementary Education, and      related ministry areas. Commitment to transformational learning, student      discipleship, and practical ministry preparation. Ability to teach effectively in multiple learning      environments, including online instruction. Strong interpersonal, communication, and mentoring      skills. Demonstrated spiritual maturity, integrity, passion,      and perseverance. Collaborative and team-oriented mindset with an      openness to diverse ministry approaches. Commitment to the authority of Scripture and      alignment with Moody Bible Institute's mission and doctrinal position. Authorized to work in the United States without      sponsorship. Preferred Earned doctorate in a related discipline. Experience leading children's, family, or      next-generation ministry initiatives within church or community settings. Demonstrated success developing, growing, or      sustaining academic and ministry programs. College-level teaching experience. Work Environment Faculty members engage in teaching, mentoring,      scholarship, and service within a Christ-centered academic environment. This position includes classroom instruction,      academic advising, committee participation, and collaboration with      colleagues across the institution. Work is performed in professional office, classroom,      and ministry-related settings. Faculty schedules generally occur Monday through      Friday, with occasional evening and weekend responsibilities. Additional Information Candidates must demonstrate alignment with Moody      Bible Institute's mission, doctrinal beliefs, and Christian values. Employees are required to affirm Moody's Statement of      Faith and adhere to Community Standards. Moody Bible Institute values diversity and seeks team      members who engage others in ways that honor its biblical foundation. Moody complies with applicable nondiscrimination laws      and, as a religious institution, requires employees to hold beliefs      consistent with its Doctrinal Statement and Community Standards. Why Join Us? At Moody, education is more than a career. It is a calling to invest in the next generation of Christian leaders. As a faculty member, you will have the opportunity to mentor students, shape future ministry practitioners, and contribute to a Christ-centered learning community committed to biblical truth and ministry excellence. In addition to meaningful work, eligible employees enjoy a comprehensive benefits package that may include: Medical, dental, and vision insurance Paid holidays, personal, and sick time Retirement benefits with institutional contributions Tuition benefits Free membership to the Solheim Athletic Center Free On-Campus Parking Professional development opportunities A collaborative and mission-driven academic community Weekly chapel services and opportunities for      spiritual growth The opportunity to influence the next generation of      Christian leaders Join us and help equip students to effectively disciple children, strengthen families, and advance the Gospel through transformational ministry around the world . Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Religion Salary: $60,000.00 - $70,000.00 Commensurate with Experience Education: Master's Degree Experience: Less than 2 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant Professor of Pharmaceutical Sciences - Medicinal Chemistry Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 26, 2026 View FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science Belhaven University Jackson, Mississippi Posted - September 10, 2026 View Payroll and Benefits Manager Asbury University Wilmore, Kentucky Posted - September 10, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Virginia Houston, Texas California Longview, Texas Alabama Ohio Texas Florida Birmingham, Alabama Azusa, California Grand Rapids, Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Charleston, South Carolina Michigan Iowa Virginia Beach, Virginia West Palm Beach, Florida Cedarville, Ohio South Carolina Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University Charleston Southern University Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Regent University Calvin University Northwestern College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Executive Education Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Computer science Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D