    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/program-director-ms-occupational-therapy-columbia-south-carolina-12618": {
      "title": "Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy in Columbia, South Carolina | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Share Save Job Apply for This Job The MS OT Program Director provides strategic, academic, and operational leadership for the Master of Occupational Therapy Program at Columbia International University. As the institution’s designated ACOTE-compliant Program Director, this role ensures program excellence through curricular integrity, accreditation compliance, faculty development and continuous quality improvement. The Program Director oversees all aspects of program administration, including curriculum design, assessment, faculty supervision, student progression, resource management and external partnerships. The Director must be able to advance the Evangelical Christian mission of the institution while fostering a culture of academic excellence, professional ethics, and student-centered learning. The CIU MS OT program is currently in the development to candidacy phase, actively pursuing initial accreditation through ACOTE. The Program Director will play a central and defining role in this accreditation process from the ground up. SOME RESPONSIBILITIES ARE: Provide overall leadership and      administrative oversight for the MSOT program in alignment with ACOTE      standards and CIU policies. Lead long‑range planning, program      evaluation, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Ensure full compliance with ACOTE      accreditation requirements, including timely submission of reports, self‑studies,      and data. Oversee curriculum development, revision,      mapping, and assessment to maintain academic rigor and professional      relevance. Manage program budgets, resource allocation,      and strategic planning for program growth. Recruit, supervise, evaluate, and mentor OT      faculty and staff, including the Fieldwork Coordinator. Coordinate faculty development, workload planning,      and instructional quality. Maintain program policies, procedures, and      documentation required for accreditation and institutional review. SOME REQIREMENTS ARE: Minimum of eight (8)      years of documented professional experience in occupational therapy,      including clinical practice. Minimum of four (4)      years of full‑time post‑baccalaureate teaching experience. Documented administrative      experience in program planning, implementation, evaluation, personnel      management, and budget/resource oversight. Earned doctoral degree      (PhD, OTD, EdD, ScD, or equivalent) from a USDE-recognized,      institutionally accredited institution CIU provides a benefits package that includes membership in the Health Plan; a 401(k) plan with match opportunity, vacation, discounted tuition Pre3K-Master’s, and more. Qualified candidates may access the FULL job description and complete the CIU Employment Application by going to the Employment page at www.ciu.edu. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Health Professions Salary: $80,000.00 - $93,000.00 Commensurate with Experience Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Part Time Doctoral Faculty - Artificial Intelligence Anderson University - SC Remote Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology or Kinesiology Simpson University Redding, California Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Azusa, California Grand Rapids, Michigan California Florida Longview, Texas Houston, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida Iowa South Carolina Michigan Ohio Charleston, South Carolina Alabama Birmingham, Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Virginia Virginia Beach, Virginia Cedarville, Ohio Texas Trending Companies Cedarville University Palm Beach Atlantic University Samford University Azusa Pacific University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Northwestern College Calvin University Charleston Southern University Regent University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Religion Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Computer science Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
