    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-education-spring-arbor-michigan-12617": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Education",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Education in Spring Arbor, Michigan | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Spring Arbor University Spring Arbor, Michigan Share Save Job Apply for This Job Full-Time Tenure-Track Faculty Spring Arbor University is seeking an individual with teaching experience who is passionate about preparing students to impact the world for Jesus Christ within the vocation of PK-12 Education. The position will begin in January 2027. Review of applicants will begin Sept 21 and continue until the position is filled. Ideally, the new faculty member would start in January 2027. POSITION DESCRIPTION Teach a full-time (24 semester hour) load of Education courses annually, with a focus on elementary education.  The successful candidate will have experience in public education and be familiar with state standards for the preparation of classroom teachers, as well as knowledge of contemporary research and evidence-based best practices in science and/or math curriculum, instruction, and assessment. The candidate should be enthusiastic about teaching and contributing to the department through advising/mentoring students, various activities related to teacher education, and working collegially with fellow faculty to support the elementary education. EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE PhD or EdD in Elementary Education or a related area is strongly preferred; master’s degree in Education, Science Education, Educational Leadership, or a related area is required. The terminal degree is required for tenure-track status to be granted. Experience as a certified elementary teacher with at least five years of successful professional teaching in K-12 schools is required, with additional years of experience in teaching or K-12 leadership preferred.  State Licensure in Michigan or another state is required. Successful college teaching experience in both traditional campus environments and online is preferred, as is experience with CAEP or other national education accreditation. QUALIFICATIONS Spring Arbor University is a community of learners distinguished by our lifelong involvement in the study and application of the liberal arts, total commitment to Jesus Christ as the perspective of learning, and critical participation in the contemporary world.  The successful candidate will be able to articulate how they would integrate the Christian faith into their discipline and will be someone who enjoys working with students and other faculty.  Individuals will exhibit a life and service that is in full accord with the Spring Arbor University Concept, the Statement of Faith, and the Community Covenant. SALARY and BENEFITS: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. Spring Arbor University provides a significant benefit package, which includes medical and life insurance and contribution to a retirement program. Experience working in multicultural academic environments is preferred, and individuals from diverse populations are encouraged to apply. Spring Arbor University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We believe it is both our moral and legal obligation to ensure that all employment practices are conducted in a nondiscriminatory manner. In compliance with Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 and other applicable federal and state statutes, all employment decisions and practices, including recruiting, hiring, training, promotion, compensation, benefits, transfers, job classification, assignments, working conditions, educational assistance, terminations, layoffs, and return from layoffs, and all other terms, conditions, and privileges of employment, will be administered without regard to race, color, ancestry, age, sex, national origin, pregnancy or childbirth, disability, military or veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal or state law. We evaluate all employees and prospective employees strictly according to the requirements of the job. As a Christian religious organization, Spring Arbor University operates under the religious exemption provided by federal law, which permits religious organizations, including educational institutions, to give employment preference to individuals who share the University's closely held religious beliefs. The University's hiring practices and equal employment policies are administered in full compliance with both federal and state law. Job Information Job Category: Education Education: Master's Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - April 29, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Associate Professor of Communication Regent University Virginia Beach, Virginia Posted - August 28, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Cybersecurity Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Texas Virginia ORANGE CITY, Iowa Cedarville, Ohio Longview, Texas California West Palm Beach, Florida Charleston, South Carolina Iowa Azusa, California Virginia Beach, Virginia Ohio Michigan Grand Rapids, Michigan Florida Birmingham, Alabama Alabama South Carolina Houston, Texas Trending Companies Calvin University Charleston Southern University Regent University Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University Houston Christian University Samford University Northwestern College LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Trending Categories Education Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Executive Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
