    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-biology-or-kinesiology-redding-california-11773": {
      "title": "Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology or Kinesiology",
      "description": "Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology or Kinesiology in Redding, California | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology or Kinesiology Simpson University Redding, California Share Save Job Apply for This Job The Department of Science and Mathematics at Simpson University invites applications for a full-time Assistant/Associate Professor of Biology and/or Kinesiology. This faculty member will teach in-person courses that may include:  Human Anatomy, Human Physiology, Global Health Issues, Applied Motor Development, Medical Terminology, and Biomechanics.  Depending on candidates’ strengths, other courses may be taught including introductory level kinesiology, biology, or chemistry courses. A commitment to the integration of faith into teaching, scholarship, and service at a Christian liberal arts institution is an essential quality of Simpson University faculty. Qualifications: ·         Doctoral degree in Biology, Kinesiology, or related discipline; M.S. degree considered ·         Demonstrated ability to teach both lecture and laboratory coursework ·         Evidence of teaching excellence utilizing a variety of teaching modalities ·         Experience working with a diverse student population and a commitment to inclusion and equity ·         A personal commitment to Christ and ability to integrate faith into teaching, scholarship, and service at a Christian liberal arts institution ·         Promising research agenda that supports undergraduate education is desirable General Expectations: ·         Personal relationship with Jesus, a vibrant Christian faith, and a commitment to Christian community; capable of sharing faith and engaging in conversations about Christ ·         Demonstrate Simpson University Values in the performance of all duties. ·         Maintain lifestyle in accordance with Simpson University Lifestyle Policy in Staff Handbook ·         Maintain the confidentiality of information, data and records ·         Properly exercise tact, diplomacy, discretion, and professional judgment ·         Demonstrate strong customer service skills in the performance of job duties ·         Demonstrate good organizational and communication skills in the performance of job duties ·         Supervises employees in accordance with Simpson University policies and procedures ·         Support the overflow needs of other departments within the respective university area ·         Perform other duties in accordance with this position as deemed necessary by the President Essential Functions: ·         Teach 12 units of undergraduate courses each fall and spring semester ·         Prepare and teach undergraduate introductory and upper-level biology and/or kinesiology courses ·         Utilize Canvas for course management and delivery of content ·         Advise and mentor undergraduate students in the biology and/or kinesiology major ·         Provide department support for curriculum design, assessment for degree program, and student recruitment ·         Serve on faculty committees ·         Attend department meetings and professional development activities ·         Ensure the timely completion of assessments, grades, and other reports Physical Requirements: - Job Title : Assistant/Associate   Professor of Biology or Kinesiology Typical Working   Conditions: (Describe environment including exposure to heat, cold, fumes, chemicals,   allergens, mold, etc.) Indoors in controlled   environment; may be exposed to chemicals and fumes associated with biology   and chemistry labs Equipment Used: (List all manual and automated equipment used in the course of performing   essential functions.) Computer, copier/printer,   mouse, keyboard, standard biology/chemistry lab equipment Essential Physical   Tasks: (List all physical tasks encountered in performing essential functions - i.e.   sitting for long periods of time using a computer, standing, climbing   ladders, etc.) Sitting for long periods of   time using a computer, standing while presenting information, setting up   equipment for lab exercises Analysis of Physical Demands to Perform Essential Functions: Key (Based on typical week): N=Never R=Rarely (Less than 1 hour per week) O=Occasional (1%-33% of time) F=Frequent (34%-66% of time) C=Constant (over 66% of time) Activity Frequency Activity Frequency N R O F C N R O F C Lifting/Carrying Twisting/Turning Under 10 lbs X Reach over shoulder X 11-20 lbs X Reach over head X 21-50 lbs X Reach outward X 51-100 lbs X Climb X Over 100 lbs X Crawl X Kneel X Pushing/Pulling Squat X Under 10 lbs X Sit X 11-20 lbs X Walk-Normal Surfaces X 21-50 lbs X Walk-Uneven Surfaces X 51-100 lbs X Walk-Slippery Surfaces X Over 100 lbs X Stand X Bend X Driving Automatic Trans X Standard Trans X Other Keyboard/Ten Key X Fingering (fine dexterity) X Handling (grasping,   holding) X Repetitive Motion –   Hands X Repetitive Motion - Feet X Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Biology/ Life Sciences Salary: $70,304 Per Year Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Ohio ORANGE CITY, Iowa Birmingham, Alabama Texas Virginia Houston, Texas Longview, Texas Michigan Grand Rapids, Michigan Virginia Beach, Virginia Alabama West Palm Beach, Florida California Cedarville, Ohio Azusa, California Charleston, South Carolina Florida South Carolina Iowa Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University Samford University Houston Christian University Northwestern College Regent University Calvin University Charleston Southern University Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Engineering Executive Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Education Faculty Careers - Computer science Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
