    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-full-professor-of-construction-management-longview-texas-12635": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA POSITION DESCRIPTION: Responsibilities include creating and offering classroom and laboratory-based courses within the recently launched Construction Management degree program, appropriate scholarship in Construction Management or a related field, assisting the program Chair in the program accreditation process, advising students, and serving on various university committees. Teaching duties include undergraduate teaching in the various Construction Management courses as well as other areas of competency. Teaching responsibilities may include both on-site and online delivery methods. QUALIFICATIONS: LeTourneau University seeks a person with an enthusiastic and contagious Christian faith who is committed to teaching and research at a small, dynamic Christian University where the integration of faith and academic excellence is paramount. The candidate must be in genuine agreement with the University’s Statement of Faith and Community Covenant for life and work at LeTourneau. Applicants must have a strong commitment to undergraduate Construction Management education with an emphasis on hands-on instruction and practical application. Applicants may be needed to teach a wide range of courses within the Construction Management program so a broad area of experience and skills is desired. Candidates must hold a Master's or PhD degree in Construction Management, engineering, business or construction-related field from an accredited program. Professional experience in the field of Construction Management is highly desired but not required. Certification and/or licensure within Construction Management, Construction, or Engineering related fields will also be considered but are not required. Candidates from broad backgrounds are encouraged to apply and will be considered based upon their potential as instructors and mentors within an undergraduate educational program. Information on the Construction Management program at LeTourneau can be found at the School of Engineering and Engineering Technology webpage: https://www.letu.edu/academics/engineering/construction-mgmt.html . SCHEDULE: The position is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position for fall and spring semesters, with the possibility of summer school and online teaching. Classes and other responsibilities are conducted primarily weekdays but may include some evening classes, independent studies, as well as some online responsibilities. Attendance will also be required at some evening and weekend events. SALARY & BENEFITS Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. DATE POSITION IS AVAILABLE: Fall 2027 PROCEDURE FOR APPLICATION OR NOMINATION : Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. Applications will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty. Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information. Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. The School of Engineering and Engineering Technology offers EAC/ABET accredited degrees in engineering with concentrations in mechanical, electrical, materials joining, biomedical, civil and computer engineering and TAC/ABET accredited degrees in engineering technology with concentrations in mechanical, electrical and materials joining. The School of Engineering and Engineering Technology has over 400 students and 25 full-time faculty. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. The 162-acre main campus is located in Longview, Texas, a progressive hub city with an MSA of over 190,000, nestled among the beautiful pine-forested hills and lakes of East Texas. It is approximately 120 miles east of Dallas, Texas and 60 miles west of Shreveport, Louisiana. See http://www.letu.edu for more information. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Engineering Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Director of Admissions Westmont College Santa Barbara, California Posted - September 15, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Michigan Virginia Grand Rapids, Michigan Longview, Texas Charleston, South Carolina Virginia Beach, Virginia South Carolina Azusa, California Texas Birmingham, Alabama Florida Ohio Iowa Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Houston, Texas California Cedarville, Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Houston Christian University Samford University Calvin University Regent University Cedarville University Charleston Southern University Palm Beach Atlantic University LeTourneau University Northwestern College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Education Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-electrical-engineering-or-engineering-technology-longview-texas-12634": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA POSITION DESCRIPTION: Responsibilities include classroom and laboratory-based teaching and research in the Engineering and/or Engineering Technology programs, advising students and serving on various university committees. Teaching duties may include undergraduate teaching in Electrical and Computer Engineering, AC/DC Electrical Circuits, Digital Electronics, Advanced Electronics, Electrical Machinery, Instrumentation and Controls, Robotics and Industrial Automation. Teaching responsibilities may include both on-site and online delivery methods. QUALIFICATIONS: LeTourneau University seeks a person with an enthusiastic and contagious Christian faith who is committed to teaching and research at a small, dynamic Christian University where the integration of faith and academic excellence is paramount. The candidate must be in genuine agreement with the University’s Statement of Faith and Community Covenant for life and work at LeTourneau. Applicants must have a strong commitment to undergraduate engineering and/or engineering technology education with a strong emphasis on laboratory instruction. Desired areas of expertise include electrical and computer engineering, electrical circuits, digital devices, plant and/or factory instrumentation and controls, as well as the modern needs of industry. Of special interest are candidates with experience in automation, robotics, and mechatronics. Candidates must hold a B.S. degree in Electrical Engineering or Electrical Engineering Technology from an ABET accredited institution and a graduate degree (M.S. minimum) in Electrical Engineering or similar. Candidates for electrical engineering should hold a terminal degree in the discipline. Industrial experience is highly desirable. Successful candidates will demonstrate evidence of outstanding potential in undergraduate teaching. Information on the Engineering and Engineering Technology programs at LeTourneau can be found at the School of Engineering and Engineering Technology web-page: http://www.letu.edu/_Academics/Engineering/index.html SCHEDULE: The position is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position for fall and spring semesters, with the possibility of summer school and online teaching. Classes and other responsibilities are conducted primarily weekdays but may include evening classes, independent studies, or online responsibilities. Attendance will also be required at some evening and weekend events. SALARY & BENEFITS Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. DATE POSITION IS AVAILABLE: Fall 2027 PROCEDURE FOR APPLICATION OR NOMINATION : Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. Applications will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty. Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information. Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. The School of Engineering and Engineering Technology offers EAC/ABET accredited degrees in engineering with concentrations in mechanical, electrical, materials joining, biomedical, civil and computer engineering and TAC/ABET accredited degrees in engineering technology with concentrations in mechanical, electrical and materials joining. The School of Engineering and Engineering Technology has over 400 students and 25 full-time faculty. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. The 162 acre main campus is located in Longview, Texas, a progressive hub city with an MSA of over 190,000, nestled among the beautiful pine-forested hills and lakes of East Texas. It is approximately 120 miles east of Dallas, Texas and 60 miles west of Shreveport, Louisiana. See http://www.letu.edu for more information. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Engineering Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Director of Admissions Westmont College Santa Barbara, California Posted - September 15, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Grand Rapids, Michigan West Palm Beach, Florida Alabama Ohio Charleston, South Carolina Virginia Beach, Virginia Florida Cedarville, Ohio Iowa Azusa, California California Houston, Texas ORANGE CITY, Iowa Michigan Virginia Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama Texas South Carolina Trending Companies LeTourneau University Northwestern College Regent University Azusa Pacific University Samford University Houston Christian University Charleston Southern University Palm Beach Atlantic University Cedarville University Calvin University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Computer science Executive Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Psychology Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
