    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/chair-department-of-teacher-education-longview-texas-12632": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Teacher Education",
      "description": "Chair, Department of Teacher Education in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA LeTourneau University, a vibrant and growing interdenominational, evangelical Christian university, known for high-quality STEM programs that attract students of outstanding academic ability, invites applications and nominations for the position of Chair and Associate/Full Professor of Education, Department of Teacher Education. This is a tenure-track position, with rank negotiable based on experience. The candidate should be an exceptional educator and leader with a strong Christian faith who will lead the Teacher Education Department within the College of Education, Arts, and Sciences (CEAS). Duties include oversight of residential and online programs and teaching courses in his or her area of education expertise. This faculty member will work closely with the CEAS dean and campus leaders to recruit and retain students, ensure quality of the curriculum, and engage with the community. This individual will be responsible for providing visionary leadership and advancing the department's mission in an ever-evolving educational landscape. This involves setting the direction and goals for the department, developing strategies, and inspiring and guiding faculty and staff in their roles. Responsibilities: •\tThe Department Chair position is an 11-month, full-time, tenure-track position with residential and/or online teaching responsibilities each semester. Duties will require flexible work hours that may include evenings, weekends, and occasional travel. •\tLead and manage all aspects of the Teacher Education Program in accordance with Texas Education Agency, State Board of Education Certification and other relevant requirements. •\tEnsure program quality through Texas Accountability System reporting, program review, accreditation support, and data-informed improvement. •\tSupervise faculty, curriculum, scheduling, and certification pathways for educator candidates. •\tOversee candidate recruitment, admissions, field experiences, progress monitoring, and certification recommendations. •\tBuild and sustain partnerships with school districts and state agencies to support educator preparation and workforce development. •\tManage departmental resources, budgeting, strategic planning, and stakeholder communication. •\tFoster collegiality and promote a positive team environment within the department. •\tEncourage innovative practices that build on the university strategic initiatives including increasing enrollment, scholarly productivity, and curricular effectiveness. Qualifications: •\tGenuine support of LeTourneau University’s Faith Statement and Community Covenant and enthusiasm for integrating faith and learning in the classroom •\tAn earned doctorate in the field of education (Ed.D. or Ph.D.) from an accredited university in any of the degree programs offered by the department •\tAn ability to teach a wide range of education courses such as science of teaching reading, differentiated instructional strategies for students with exceptionalities, and/or education methods courses for elementary and secondary levels •\tA valid Texas teacher certificate (or eligible to apply for a Texas teacher certificate) with a minimum of three years EC-12 public-school teaching experience. Principal certification is strongly desired. •\tDemonstrated experience working with programs leading to initial and/or professional teaching certifications through state examinations •\tDemonstrated excellence in teaching using evidence-based research practices •\tExperience with EC-12 partnerships and clinical practice in teacher education •\tDemonstrated effective leadership experiences in higher education and/or EC-12 environments including effective communication and positive academic leadership skills •\tKnowledge of the Texas Education Agency accreditation requirements Salary and Benefits: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. Date Position is Available: Summer or Fall 2027 Application Procedure: Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. Applications will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty. Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information.  Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. About the University: LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Education Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Chair of Mechanical Engineering Houston Christian University Houston, Texas Posted - August 7, 2026 View Full-time Faculty, Marriage and Family Therapy - College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Dean, School of Ministry Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 17, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Azusa, California Alabama Houston, Texas Cedarville, Ohio South Carolina Charleston, South Carolina West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Florida California Virginia Beach, Virginia Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Longview, Texas Grand Rapids, Michigan Iowa Virginia Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Trending Companies Houston Christian University Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Calvin University Charleston Southern University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Cedarville University Northwestern College Samford University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Health Professions Education Faculty Careers - Mathematics Executive Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
