    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-sport-studies-longview-texas-12631": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA LeTourneau University, a vibrant and growing interdenominational, evangelical Christian university, known for high-quality STEM programs that attract students of outstanding academic ability, invites applications and nominations for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies, Department of Human Performance & Sport Studies. This is a tenure-track position with rank negotiable based on experience. This faculty member will teach a range of kinesiology & sport studies courses with an emphasis on sport studies at undergraduate level. This position is designed for a dynamic faculty member who is passionate about teaching, mentoring, and preparing students for careers in sport-related fields through experiential learning, industry engagement, and faith integration. The ideal candidate should have excellent team-building skills and the interest and experience to provide growth to the Department of Human Performance & Sport Studies. Research and teaching experience are highly desired. The position is for nine months with the possibility of summer teaching. Classes and other responsibilities are conducted primarily weekdays but could include some evening classes and independent studies. Attendance will also be required at some evening and weekend events. Responsibilities: •\tTeach undergraduate courses in sport-related areas such as sport management, sport communication, sport marketing, sport sociology, sport ethics, and various other sport studies topics •\tContribute to the development and growth of the Human Performance & Sport Studies program •\tAdvise and mentor students in academic, professional, and spiritual development •\tIntentionally integrate faith in the classroom and in one-on-one discipleship in a meaningful way •\tEngage in experiential learning initiatives (e.g., internships, industry partnerships, event-based learning such as Final Four or Super Bowl opportunities) •\tMaintain an active agenda of scholarship or professional engagement appropriate to the discipline •\tParticipate in departmental, university, and professional service Qualifications: •\tEarned doctorate in Sport Management, Sport Studies, Kinesiology, or a related field required •\tDemonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching •\tAbility to teach across multiple sport-related disciplines depending on program needs •\tStrong communication and interpersonal skills •\tProfessional or applied experience in the sport industry preferred Salary and Benefits: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. Date Position is Available: Fall 2027 Procedure for Application or Nomination: Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. The review process will begin as early as October 15th, 2026, and all applications received by October 30th, 2026, will receive full consideration. Applications after that date will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty. Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information.  Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. About LeTourneau University LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Other Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Payroll and Benefits Manager Asbury University Wilmore, Kentucky Posted - September 10, 2026 View FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science Belhaven University Jackson, Mississippi Posted - September 10, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Biology Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View Instructor of Mathematics Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Florida Longview, Texas Azusa, California Ohio Houston, Texas Grand Rapids, Michigan Alabama Birmingham, Alabama California Cedarville, Ohio Virginia Beach, Virginia Michigan Iowa Charleston, South Carolina Texas ORANGE CITY, Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Virginia South Carolina Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Palm Beach Atlantic University Cedarville University Regent University Calvin University Northwestern College LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Charleston Southern University Samford University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Mathematics Executive Education Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
