    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/director-of-finance-lisle-il-illinois-12630": {
      "title": "Director of Finance",
      "description": "Director of Finance in Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Share Save Job Apply for This Job Position Information Department: Business Office / Administration FLSA Status: Exempt, Full-Time Reports To: President To Apply: Email Resume and Cover Letter to [email protected] Effective Date: 10/01/2026 Position Summary The Director of Finance at Northern Seminary provides strategic as well as working leadership across the  institution's finance functions. This role is responsible for ensuring the financial health, regulatory compliance, and  operational effectiveness of the Seminary. The Director of Finance partners closely with the President and senior  leadership team to advance the Seminary's mission through sound stewardship of resources, people, and institutional  processes. As a member of the leadership team, this individual embodies the core values of Northern Seminary and  contributes to a culture of integrity, collaboration, and servant leadership. Duties and Responsibilities Finance & Accounting ● Provide overall leadership and strategic direction for all financial operations of the Seminary, including  accounting, budgeting, financial reporting, and forecasting. ● Supervise financial reporting, billing, collections, student accounts, AP/AR, payroll, and budget preparation. ● Ensure full compliance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and nonprofit accounting  standards, including fund accounting requirements. ● Oversee preparation and presentation of monthly, quarterly, and annual financial reports to the President,  Finance Committee, and Board of Trustees. ● Lead the annual budget development process in collaboration with department leaders; monitor financial  performance against budget and advise leadership on variances and trends. ● Provide multi-year financial forecasting and scenario planning to support strategic decision-making ● Advise the President on financial implications of enrollment trends, tuition pricing, and program decisions ● Manage daily cash flow to ensure sufficient liquidity for Seminary operations and invest surplus funds  appropriately. Tracking unrestricted and restricted resources available. ● Serve as the primary liaison with independent external auditors; oversee preparation of all audit work papers,  updated policies, procedures, and ensure timely completion of the annual audit. ● Maintain the Seminary's internal control framework, including segregation of duties and safeguarding of assets. ● Maintain Title IV compliance and manage the federal loan and Northern Student Loan programs, including  preparation and submission of loan requests, deferment forms, and compliance reporting. ● Serve as liaison with endowment managers to maintain accurate records of restricted and unrestricted funds;  collaborate with leadership on endowment strategy and distributions. ● Oversee annuity reporting and provide support to the letter of credit process. ● Collaborate with department leaders to review and assess financial viability of all grant submissions. ● Advise the President, Board, and senior leadership on cash flow, investment priorities, and financial objectives. ● Provide financial analysis and data to support the President's planning processes. ● Analyze market trends and opportunities for financial viability and organizational growth.  Supervisory Responsibilities ● Directly supervises the accounting and operational staff. ● Recruits, hires, and evaluates direct reports; coordinates performance review processes. Required Skills and Abilities ● Expert knowledge of nonprofit accounting, fund accounting, and GAAP financial reporting. ● Experience managing a multi-million dollar budget. ● Strong understanding of regulatory compliance in a higher education context. ● Proficiency in accounting software (QuickBooks), student information systems (Populi), HRIS platforms  (Paylocity), and Microsoft Office Suite. ● Ability to develop, implement, and assess internal controls and institutional policies. ● Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and strategic thinking skills. ● Strong written and oral communication; ability to present complex financial data to non-financial audiences. ● Demonstrated ability to manage multiple high-priority projects simultaneously. ● High level of integrity, discretion, and ability to handle confidential information. ● Ability to build collaborative, trust-based relationships across all levels of the institution.  Education and Experience ● Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field required; Master's  degree (MBA, MPA, or similar) preferred. CPA designation strongly preferred. ● Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience in finance and accounting, with at least  three (3) years in a senior leadership role. ● Minimum of three (3) years of experience in nonprofit or higher education financial management. ● Demonstrated experience overseeing or managing human resources functions. ● Experience with Title IV federal financial aid compliance preferred. ● Experience working with a Board of Trustees/Directors and presenting financial information at the board level. ● Experience working in a faith-based or mission-driven institution preferred. Core Values The Director of Finance will reflect and advance the core values of Northern Seminary: ● International, Interracial, Intercultural, and Mutual — Actively supporting a diverse and inclusive institution  that reflects the breadth of Christ's church. ● Pastoral/Mission Mindset — Understanding and supporting the mission-driven nature of theological education. ● Servant Leadership — Approaching all responsibilities with integrity, humility, and a commitment to serving  students, staff, and the broader community. ● Teachable — Maintaining openness, growth, and continued learning in relationship with God and the world.  Working Conditions ● Hybrid office environment; ability to work in a dynamic environment. ● Attendance at staff meetings (monthly), Board meetings, Finance Committee meetings, and other leadership  gatherings as required. ● Extended periods of sitting and computer work. ● Must be able to lift up to 25 pounds occasionally. ● Must provide own form of reliable transportation. ● Some remote or flexible work arrangements may be available in alignment with institutional policy. ● Must comply with the Seminary Faith and Community Standard statements. Job Information Job Category: Accounting / Finance Salary: $110,000 - $125,000 Per Year Education: Bachelor's Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - April 29, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Director of Human Resources MidAmerica Nazarene University Olathe, Kansas Posted - August 28, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Virginia Beach, Virginia Iowa Charleston, South Carolina Birmingham, Alabama Texas Longview, Texas Alabama Ohio Florida South Carolina Virginia ORANGE CITY, Iowa Michigan Azusa, California Grand Rapids, Michigan Cedarville, Ohio Houston, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida California Trending Companies Regent University Houston Christian University Palm Beach Atlantic University Calvin University LeTourneau University Samford University Charleston Southern University Northwestern College Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University Trending Categories Education Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Mathematics Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/director-of-doctor-of-ministry-houston-texas-12561": {
      "title": "Director of Doctor of Ministry",
      "description": "Director of Doctor of Ministry in Houston, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Director of Doctor of Ministry Houston Christian University Houston, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job We are seeking a full-time faculty member who will lead our Doctor of Ministry program. The faculty member will have leadership and ministry experience, be dedicated to training others for service in ministry, and have expertise and a terminal degree in one of the following areas: Practical      Theology Biblical      Studies Cultural      Apologetics Job Responsibilities: Provide      vision and leadership for the Doctor of Ministry program Promote      the doctoral program and effectively recruit new DMin students Oversee      the operation of the Doctor of Ministry, including planning for the 1-week      intensives each semester and managing supervisory assignments Be      a point of contact for prospective students interested in Doctor of      Ministry Provide      mentorship and advising for current doctoral students Advance      the Doctor of Ministry program through church partnerships, adjunct      recruitment, and other proactive initiatives Lead      program accreditation maintenance and renewal Work      with the chair of the Department of Theology In      conjunction with the Dean’s office, oversee the DMin budget, including the      awarding of the Cole Scholarship. Teach      the equivalent of a 4-4 load, with a 2-2 course reduction for      administrative duties. The successful candidate will: Provide      excellent teaching to School of Christian Thought students in a variety of      delivery formats; Actively      integrate the Christian faith in teaching; Actively      engage in scholarly work in their related discipline; Participate      in various service activities to the School, University, and community;      and, Maintain      an active Christian faith and church participation. Qualifications: Candidates      should have an earned PhD or DMin in a related field; Professional      experience within the candidate’s discipline or in a related field will be      an advantage; and Substantial      experience in organizational leadership and ministry. Candidates      must affirm HCU’s statement of faith encompassed in the university preamble and Ten Pillars .      This commitment must be reaffirmed annually. HCU      seeks candidates with an active Christian faith who are willing to      integrate faith and learning in the classroom. The candidate must be able      to document an excellent teaching record and provide evidence of scholarly      interests and achievements. Job Information Job Category: Education Related Jobs Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Dean, School of Ministry Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - September 16, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Part Time Doctoral Faculty - Artificial Intelligence Anderson University - SC Remote Posted - September 15, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Iowa Alabama Azusa, California Grand Rapids, Michigan Charleston, South Carolina Cedarville, Ohio South Carolina Virginia Houston, Texas Florida California Michigan Virginia Beach, Virginia Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Trending Companies Calvin University Cedarville University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Azusa Pacific University Palm Beach Atlantic University Charleston Southern University Regent University Samford University Northwestern College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
