igibility, timing, sponsorship, and funding considerations under current U.S. immigration and visa requirements. TO APPLY Complete the online application process and attach the following: A one-page letter of application that addresses your ability to fulfill the requirements and responsibilities of the position A 250 to 500-word statement describing your Christian faith and explaining your interest in teaching and scholarship at a Reformed Christian University Your full curriculum vitae (CV) TIMELINE Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Direct questions to Scott Rush, Accounting, Finance and Analytics Chair, via email at [email protected] . FAITH and EDUCATIONAL COMMITMENT 1. Commitment to the educational mission of Calvin as a Christian liberal arts university affiliated with the Christian Reformed Church. 2. A commitment to the Christian faith and to the integration of faith, learning, and student development. DIVERSITY COMMITMENT Demonstrated awareness and commitment to effectively establishing relationships and positive communication across multiple dimensions of diversity including, but not limited to, race, gender, physical limitations, class, or religious perspectives. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Business Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs School of Business Tenure-Track Finance Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 16, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Director of Finance Northern Seminary Lisle, IL, Illinois (Hybrid) Posted - September 14, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (