    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-of-strategic-communication-orange-city-iowa-12642": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication in ORANGE CITY, Iowa | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Share Save Job Apply for This Job Northwestern College seeks applicants for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of assistant professor in our English and communications department to begin August 2027. Interested candidates who have already attained higher rank may also inquire. The successful candidate can expect to teach courses in communications with specific emphases in strategic communication and public relations. The teaching load for this position is 24 credit-hours per academic year, normally three to four courses per semester. Responsibilities include teaching introductory and intermediate courses in communication, along with advanced courses in public relations. Required Qualifications: Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a communications field. Near-completion ABDs are also welcome to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate a keen ability to connect with our vibrant undergraduate students, sustain an active research program, build connections with local practitioners, and contribute to the life of the institution through faculty committees and other co-curricular service. Preferred Qualifications: While the primary focus of this position is strategic communication, strongest consideration will be given to those who also have additional experience in public relations. Our Department: Northwestern’s English and communications department celebrates professional and multimodal communication alongside literary study and theoretical practice. As the home for our journalism minor, our student newspaper ( The Beacon ), and our multimedia literary arts magazine ( The Archive ), our department promotes how storytelling flourishes in a variety of contexts and media platforms. Our current majors include public relations , writing and digital media , and English teaching . Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our calling to be a Christian academic community. Apply online and send a current CV and a letter of interest to [email protected] . In your letter, (1) summarize your teaching experience; (2) describe your scholarly trajectory; and (3) discuss how our Christian Identity Statement would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship. Review of applications will begin on Oct. 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Northwestern College seeks applicants for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of assistant professor in our English and communications department to begin August 2027. Interested candidates who have already attained higher rank may also inquire. The successful candidate can expect to teach courses in communications with specific emphases in strategic communication and public relations. The teaching load for this position is 24 credit-hours per academic year, normally three to four courses per semester. Responsibilities include teaching introductory and intermediate courses in communication, along with advanced courses in public relations. Required Qualifications: Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a communications field. Near-completion ABDs are also welcome to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate a keen ability to connect with our vibrant undergraduate students, sustain an active research program, build connections with local practitioners, and contribute to the life of the institution through faculty committees and other co-curricular service. Preferred Qualifications: While the primary focus of this position is strategic communication, strongest consideration will be given to those who also have additional experience in public relations. Our Department: Northwestern’s English and communications department celebrates professional and multimodal communication alongside literary study and theoretical practice. As the home for our journalism minor, our student newspaper ( The Beacon ), and our multimedia literary arts magazine ( The Archive ), our department promotes how storytelling flourishes in a variety of contexts and media platforms. Our current majors include public relations , writing and digital media , and English teaching . Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our calling to be a Christian academic community. Apply online below and send a current CV and a letter of interest to [email protected] . In your letter, (1) summarize your teaching experience; (2) describe your scholarly trajectory; and (3) discuss how our Christian Identity Statement would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship. Review of applications will begin on Oct. 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Communication/ Design/ Media Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: Less than 2 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Community Nursing Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Faculty and Program Director - B.A. in Animation and Visual Effects Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Anderson, South Carolina Virginia Cedarville, Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Ohio Charleston, South Carolina Florida Azusa, California Michigan Houston, Texas Iowa Grand Rapids, Michigan California Longview, Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia Texas South Carolina West Palm Beach, Florida ORANGE CITY, Iowa Alabama Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Cedarville University LeTourneau University Charleston Southern University Samford University Northwestern College Anderson University - SC Houston Christian University Calvin University Azusa Pacific University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Other Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Mathematics Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Executive Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Psychology Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
