    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/dean-school-of-ministry-west-palm-beach-florida-12504": {
      "title": "Dean, School of Ministry in West Palm Beach, Florida",
      "description": "Dean, School of Ministry in West Palm Beach, Florida | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Dean, School of Ministry Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Share Save Job Apply for This Job About Palm Beach Atlantic University Founded in 1968, Palm Beach Atlantic University is a Christ-centered university experiencing a season of remarkable growth, momentum, and expanding influence. PBA now enrolls more than 4,200 students across more than 100 academic programs and draws students from all 50 states and more than 80 countries. As a comprehensive Christian university, PBA is an academically rigorous, classically evangelical, and non denominational university. Our theologically conservative stance is articulated through PBA’s Guiding Principles and values statements. Located in downtown West Palm Beach, Florida, PBA has recently undergone a remarkable period of expansion, with seven-fold increase in applications over the last six years, simultaneous with reiterating our long standing orthodox Christian stance. Rooted in a Christ-first mission and guided by biblical conviction, the University stands at a defining moment, expanding its campus footprint and elevating its role as a premier Christian university shaping the next generation of healthcare, marketplace, and ministry leaders. The School of Ministry The School of Ministry plays a vital role as the spiritual center of a vibrant university and community. Within the School of Ministry, PBA’s faith-based programming and spiritual and theological instruction prepare our students to serve as the next generation of pastors, scholars, chaplains, missionaries, and marketplace leaders grounded in Scripture and the historic Christian faith. The academic strength and innovation of the School of Ministry is supported by a strong grouping of grants totaling over $17.5M. These grants extend the mission of the school in the following areas: Community-based chaplaincy      education Multi-ethnic church leadership      education Established a new network of      churches in South FL for education resourcing and community. The school is accredited by the Commission on Accrediting of the Association of Theological Schools (ATS) and holds accredited status in good standing. Its programs span the baccalaureate through the doctorate, offered in both residential and online formats, and are anchored by a curriculum that integrates the study of the Bible, theology, theological languages, and practical ministry. PBA’s apologetics program is among the finest in the country, and the School’s Accelerated Ministry Program allows students to earn a B.A. and M.Div. in as few as five years. The Role The Dean reports to the Provost and serves on the University’s senior academic leadership team. The Dean is responsible for all aspects of the School’s academic life and culture and will cast a compelling vision that aligns with the University’s overall mission and continue to strengthen the School of Ministry as the heart of PBA’s spiritual and intellectual formation. This is a high-trust, high-expectation role that calls for an executive leader who can serve as builder, strategist, shepherd, and ambassador, modeling transparent leadership, collaborative decision-making, and unwavering commitment to the university and training the next generation of Christian leaders. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Lead faculty recruitment,      development, and evaluation, cultivating scholar-teacher-practitioners who      unite rigorous scholarship with a pastoral heart by hiring well, mentoring      wisely, and evaluating with consistency and care. The dean is tasked with      hiring rising star faculty and ministry mentors. Steward strategic planning,      accreditation, and academic quality, sustaining ATS accreditation and      curricular quality across residential and online programs from the      baccalaureate through the doctorate. Work with university leadership to      build strong public and private partnerships to fund ministry scholarships      in the wake of federal means testing for student loans. Direct curricular innovation,      enrollment strategy, and financial stewardship, advancing student outcomes      and program health (academic and fiscal) across the School’s      undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral offerings. Continue to innovate with      grant support and prepare pastors who can lead well. Champion faculty scholarship as a      missional calling, advancing both the academic reputation of the School      and the spiritual influence of its faculty, staff, and students in service      to the Church and the academy. Cultivate church, denominational,      and ministry partnerships, connecting students to vocational formation and      the School to the wider body of Christ. Identify ministerial and academic      leaders to cultivate a community of mentoring. Partner with colleagues in      enrollment, marketing, and advancement to fuel sustainable growth and      strengthen the operational excellence that supports the success of the      School and provide vibrant pastoral leaders needed globally today. Represent the School externally      to the Church and the academy, engaging pastors, donors, alumni, and      ministry partners committed to excellence in Christian theological      education in a changing world. Strategic Leadership Priorities The next Dean will be called to cast and implement a compelling vision that aligns with the University’s overall mission and strengthens the School of Ministry. Rooted in Scripture and the historic evangelical tradition, the Dean will serve as builder, strategist, shepherd, and ambassador. Cast a compelling vision that      unites the biblical, theological, and practical disciplines, fostering      meaningful integration across the School while respecting the depth of      each field and forming students in both conviction and character. Cultivate a culture of faculty      excellence and collegiality. Champion faculty scholarship as a      missional calling that serves both the academy and the Church. • Steward      ATS accreditation and program health across residential and online      formats, from the baccalaureate through the doctorate. Cultivate church, denominational,      and ministry partnerships that deepen vocational formation and extend the      School’s witness. Lead with authenticity,      transparency, and a clear eye toward building trust across the School and      the University. Partner with enrollment,      marketing, and advancement to fuel sustainable growth, bringing systems      thinking and executional follow-through to align resources, space, and      workload to strategy. Represent the School as a      thoughtful public voice and institutional ambassador to the Church and the      academy, engaging donors, alumni, and strategic partners. QUALIFICATIONS Earned Ph.D. or terminal degree      in a biblical, theological, or religious-studies discipline, with a record      of scholarship sufficient for appointment as full professor; an M.Div. is      strongly preferred. Prior leadership experience at      the dean, associate dean, or department chair level. Demonstrated success leading      faculty, managing budgets, and overseeing academic and financial      operations. Experience with accreditation      (ATS familiarity a plus), faculty governance, academic innovation, and      institutional complexity. Capable of leading vibrant teams      of faculty, staff, and students. • Experience with grant development,      donor cultivation, or external partnership development. PERSONAL CHARACTERISTICS A mature and deeply rooted      Christian faith in alignment with the mission, vision, values, and      commitments of PBA. Deep experience and maturity as a      Christian leader in both ministry and the academy. A demonstrated commitment to      integrating faith, scholarship, and ministry practice. Relational intelligence,      emotional maturity, and institutional humility. An authentic and compelling      communicator who leads with transparency and builds trust. A builder and shepherd with a      high view of academic calling, collegial culture, and the Church. Applications and Nominations Palm Beach Atlantic University invites applications, nominations, and expressions of interest for this opportunity to lead the spiritual heart of a rising Christian university. All conversations and submissions will be handled with complete discretion. Please send a CV and a letter describing your faith commitment, leadership approach, and qualifications for the role, addressed to the School of Ministry Dean Search Committee. Nominations, expressions of interest, and applications should be submitted to PBADeanSearch@pba.edu . The priority application date is October 1, 2026. Learn More Here: Dean of the School of Ministry Job Information Job Category: Education Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General) Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Civil Engineering Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Ohio South Carolina Florida Charleston, South Carolina Cedarville, Ohio Longview, Texas Texas Alabama Birmingham, Alabama Virginia Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Azusa, California Michigan California Virginia Beach, Virginia Grand Rapids, Michigan Houston, Texas ORANGE CITY, Iowa Trending Companies LeTourneau University Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University Charleston Southern University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Regent University Calvin University Northwestern College Samford University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Health Professions Education Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Executive Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Engineering Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713 Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
