    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/part-time-doctoral-faculty-artificial-intelligence-12639": {
      "title": "Part Time Doctoral Faculty",
      "description": "Part Time Doctoral Faculty - Artificial Intelligence in Remote | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Part Time Doctoral Faculty - Artificial Intelligence Anderson University - SC Remote Share Save Job Apply for This Job Anderson University’s International Graduate School invites applications for part-time doctoral faculty in Artificial Intelligence to teach in the University’s Doctor of Education (Ed.D.) in Leadership and Artificial Intelligence. The Ed.D. in Leadership and Artificial Intelligence is a professional doctorate designed for experienced professionals who will lead organizations through the opportunities, challenges, and transformations created by artificial intelligence. The program integrates advanced leadership study with artificial intelligence, digital transformation, cybersecurity, ethics, organizational innovation, and applied doctoral research. Anderson University is particularly interested in scholar-practitioners and accomplished AI professionals who combine appropriate doctoral credentials with significant real-world experience in artificial intelligence and related technologies. Because artificial intelligence is a rapidly developing field, Anderson University values both academic preparation and substantive professional experience. Candidates are not required to hold a doctorate specifically titled “Artificial Intelligence”. However, candidates must possess an earned terminal degree and demonstrate significant academic and/or professional expertise appropriate to the doctoral course or courses they would teach. Areas of Teaching Need Anderson University is recruiting faculty qualified to teach one or more of the following courses: LEAI 701 – Foundations of AI: History and Development LEAI 740 – Machine Learning and Generative AI LEAI 750 – AI Ethics and Responsible Use LEAI 760 – Cybersecurity, Privacy, and AI Risk Management LEAI 770 – Leading Change through Digital Transformation and AI Innovation LEAI 780 – Applied Doctoral Research Seminar in Leadership and AI LEAI 790 – Capstone Project Minimum Qualifications Candidates must possess: An earned terminal degree (Ph.D., Ed.D., D.Sc., D.B.A., D.Eng., D.C.S., or other appropriate doctorate) from an appropriately accredited institution. Graduate education, scholarship, research, and/or significant professional expertise related to the course or courses to be taught. Demonstrated knowledge of contemporary artificial intelligence and its application within organizations. The ability to teach and mentor students at the doctoral level in an academically rigorous and professionally relevant environment. The ability to teach effectively in online, hybrid, and intensive-residency formats. A commitment to supporting the mission and values of Anderson University. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates demonstrating one or more of the following: Significant professional experience implementing or leading artificial intelligence initiatives in business, government, healthcare, education, technology, cybersecurity, consulting, nonprofit organizations, or other sectors. Expertise in generative AI, large language models, machine learning, AI-enabled analytics, AI agents and workflows, predictive systems, or emerging AI technologies. Experience with enterprise AI implementation, digital transformation, technology strategy, organizational innovation, or AI-enabled decision-making. Expertise in AI governance, ethics, privacy, cybersecurity, regulatory compliance, responsible AI, or AI risk management. Graduate or doctoral-level teaching experience. Experience supervising dissertations, doctoral research, applied research, or executive-level capstone projects. Evidence of continuing engagement with the rapidly evolving AI field through scholarship, applied projects, consulting, industry leadership, professional certifications, professional development, or other substantive activities. The Scholar-Practitioner We Seek The Ed.D. in Leadership and Artificial Intelligence is a professional doctorate. Anderson University therefore seeks faculty who can connect doctoral scholarship with contemporary organizational practice. Ideal candidates may include senior technology executives, artificial intelligence and data science leaders, cybersecurity professionals, consultants, researchers, entrepreneurs, government technology leaders, or experienced academics who possess both an appropriate terminal degree and demonstrated expertise in artificial intelligence. Of particular interest are professionals who have participated directly in the development, implementation, management, governance, or strategic use of artificial intelligence within organizations. Our faculty should help doctoral students understand not simply what artificial intelligence can do, but how leaders can evaluate, implement, govern, secure, and responsibly use AI to improve and transform organizations. Teaching in the Ed.D. Program Faculty members will work with experienced professionals pursuing a practice-oriented doctoral degree. Depending upon course assignment, responsibilities may include: Teaching doctoral courses in online and hybrid formats. Connecting current AI developments with leadership and organizational practice. Using case studies, applied projects, simulations, and contemporary organizational challenges. Mentoring doctoral students in applied research. Advising students as they translate research into organizational solutions. Participating, when appropriate, in the Responsible AI Leadership Capstone, through which students address significant workplace, organizational, industry, or societal challenges using responsible applications of artificial intelligence. Faculty teaching research and capstone courses may also guide students in research design, organizational analysis, implementation strategies, evaluation, and professional presentation of doctoral-level work. About our Commitment to Fairness in Employment Anderson University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, age, religion, genetic information, veteran or military status, or any other basis on which the University is prohibited from discrimination under the local, state, or federal law, in its employment or in the provision of its services, including but not limited to its programs and activities, admissions, educational policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other University-administered programs. As a Christian institution of higher education, Anderson University is entitled to certain religious accommodations under federal and state law, including Title IX of the Education Amendments Act and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act. For questions or concerns contact the Office of Human Resources at hr@andersonuniversity.edu . Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Other Position Type: Part Time Related Jobs Campus Staff Minister - Washington University-St. Louis (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA St. Louis, Missouri Posted - September 15, 2026 View Part Time Faculty - Studio Art Anderson University - SC Anderson, South Carolina Posted - September 16, 2026 View Campus Staff Minister - Emory University (Graduate & Faculty Ministry) InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Atlanta, Georgia Posted - September 15, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Posted - September 15, 2026 View Dean, School of Ministry Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - September 16, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Houston, Texas Cedarville, Ohio Virginia Longview, Texas Alabama Virginia Beach, Virginia Charleston, South Carolina Azusa, California Florida Grand Rapids, Michigan Birmingham, Alabama South Carolina Michigan Ohio California ORANGE CITY, Iowa Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Trending Companies Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University Charleston Southern University Regent University Calvin University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University Northwestern College Trending Categories Executive Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713 Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
