    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/grants-and-research-coordinator-lake-wales-florida-12638": {
      "title": "Grants and Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Grants and Research Coordinator in Lake Wales, Florida | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Grants and Research Coordinator Warner University Lake Wales, Florida Share Save Job Apply for This Job Description Position Summary: This position supports the Advancement Office by identifying, researching, and cultivating funding opportunities that advance the mission of the institution. This position is responsible for managing the grant lifecycle, conducting donor and prospect research, maintaining accurate constituent records, assisting with stewardship reporting, and supporting strategic fundraising initiatives. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, an excellent writer, and passionate about advancing Christian higher education through philanthropy. Preference will be given to alumni of Warner University and individuals who have an exceptionally close connection to the institution and/or community. The successful candidate will both understand and value the cultural role of evangelical Christian higher education, and he or she will understand the importance of Warner University in central Florida and beyond. The candidate must affirm and support the University’s official Statement of Faith. The selected candidate must be energetic about the University’s goal of distinguishing itself in the higher-education industry through commitment to historic biblical values. Responsibilities: Research and identify foundation, corporate, government, and private grant opportunities aligned with institutional priorities. Develop and maintain an annual grants calendar with application deadlines, reporting requirements, and stewardship activities. Write, edit, and coordinate compelling grant proposals, letters of inquiry, budgets, and supporting documentation. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and administrators to gather program information, budgets, outcomes, and evaluation data. Prepare timely grant reports and stewardship updates demonstrating donor impact and compliance with grant requirements. Monitor grant expenditures and coordinate with the Business Office to ensure compliance with grant restrictions. Conduct prospect research on individuals, foundations, corporations, and organizations to identify new funding opportunities. Prepare donor profiles, briefing materials, and prospect summaries for the President and Vice President for Advancement. Analyze giving history, wealth indicators, philanthropic interests, and engagement opportunities. Assist in identifying prospective major gift, planned giving, and annual fund donors. Support Advancement with regard to scholarship stewardship, endowment acknowledgments letters , Board of Trustee meetings, and engagement with donors and prospects. Support the team by performing tasks related to organization and strong communication. Assist with advancement projects as needed. Qualifications Associate degree in a related field (bachelor’s degree preferred) The ability to locate and utilize relevant data Commitment to and an understanding of utilizing and providing clean and accurate data Minimum 2 years relevant professional experience in a similar position while demonstrating responsibility for data entry, database management, and gift processing Experience using reporting tools to research and produce reports as requested Experience accepting and recording gifts in a similar not-for-profit organization Experience utilizing Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge or Raiser’s Edge NXT or comparable database tool Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including a professional telephone manner Demonstrated experience in professionally handling sensitive and confidential information Procedure: Candidates must submit the following: Letter of Interest Resume Faith Statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the University’s official Statement of Faith: ( https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/ ) Name, title, and contact information for 3-5 professional references Applications will not be reviewed unless all requested materials are submitted. Applications are being accepted and will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Preferably, the chosen candidate would start in September 2026. Salary will be contingent on qualifications and experience. Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/ Fundraising Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Community Nursing Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Director of Assessment, Academic Affairs University of Northwestern - St. Paul St. Paul, Minnesota Posted - August 31, 2026 View Associate Registrar for Records & Student Services Bethel University St. Paul, Minnesota Posted - September 1, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Associate Professor of Communication Regent University Virginia Beach, Virginia Posted - August 28, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Grand Rapids, Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa South Carolina Cedarville, Ohio Longview, Texas Texas West Palm Beach, Florida California Iowa Azusa, California Virginia Beach, Virginia Charleston, South Carolina Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Houston, Texas Florida Alabama Michigan Virginia Trending Companies Regent University Calvin University Samford University Cedarville University Northwestern College Charleston Southern University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Azusa Pacific University Palm Beach Atlantic University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Psychology Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
