    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-in-accounting-upland-indiana-12684": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track in Accounting",
      "description": "Tenure-Track in Accounting in Upland, Indiana | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure-Track in Accounting Taylor University Upland, Indiana Share Save Job Apply for This Job Taylor University is seeking applications and nominations for distinguished candidates to teach in the Department of Business in Accounting.  This is a tenure-track position beginning August 2027. Appointment of rank and salary are dependent upon qualifications and experience. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Mission and Commitment Taylor's mission is to develop servant-leaders marked with a passion to minister Christ’s redemptive love, grace, and truth to a world in need. As a community, Taylor faculty, staff, and students commit to living out Christ’s love and truth in the here and now. We worship together, serve one another, and grow in faith as we learn in the classroom, on the field, at chapel, and anywhere else we’re doing Life Together. Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach a variety of accounting courses based on the candidate’s credentials and experience (e.g., Intermediate Accounting, Cost Accounting, Advanced Accounting, Auditing, Accounting Analytics, Integrated Accounting Systems). The normal teaching load is 24 hours per academic year.  Scholarly activity, professional service, student advising, faculty governance responsibilities, and chapel attendance are also expected. Typical Qualifications PhD or DBA in Accounting or a closely related field is preferred. A strong interest in undergraduate teaching is required, and previous teaching, and/or online course delivery are desired. Professional work experience and credentials are also required. Candidates must have a personal, vibrant faith and Christian walk, and be strongly committed to the educational mission and evangelical Christian orientation of the University. About the Department The Business Department consists of 10 full-time faculty members and is an ACBSP accredited program focused on preparing students for Kingdom Impact in business. The department offers majors in accounting, entrepreneurship and economic development, finance, management, marketing, and sport management, and both Bachelor of Arts and Bachelor of Science degrees. There are approximately 500 students enrolled, making business the largest major group on campus. All business majors have a practicum requirement, and the curriculum includes project and experiential learning components. The faculty enjoy a strong collegial relationship and smaller classes that encourage student mentoring and discipleship. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Business Related Jobs Tenure-Track in Economics Taylor University Upland, Indiana Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Finance Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View School of Business Tenure-Track Business Analytics Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 16, 2026 View School of Business Tenure-Track Accounting Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 16, 2026 View School of Business Marketing Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 16, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Trending Locations Pennsylvania Grand Rapids, Michigan South Carolina Azusa, California Charleston, South Carolina Cedarville, Ohio California Redding, California Ohio Iowa St. Paul, Minnesota Wheaton, Illinois Texas Chicago, Illinois Houston, Texas Florida Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama Anderson, South Carolina Michigan Minnesota ORANGE CITY, Iowa Alabama Illinois Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania West Palm Beach, Florida Trending Companies Northwestern College Anderson University - SC Wheaton College Azusa Pacific University Samford University Cedarville University Messiah University Palm Beach Atlantic University Simpson University Calvin University Charleston Southern University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Moody Bible Institute InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Education Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Executive Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Accounting / Finance Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Ou