    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-in-special-education-upland-indiana-12683": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track in Special Education",
      "description": "Tenure-Track in Special Education in Upland, Indiana | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure-Track in Special Education Taylor University Upland, Indiana Share Save Job Apply for This Job Taylor University is seeking applications and nominations of distinguished candidates for a tenure-track faculty position in Education beginning in August 2027. Rank and salary are dependent upon qualifications and experience. Mission and Commitment Taylor's mission is to develop servant-leaders marked with a passion to minister Christ’s redemptive love, grace, and truth to a world in need. As a community, Taylor faculty, staff, and students commit to living out Christ’s love and truth in the here and now. We worship together, serve one another, and grow in faith as we learn in the classroom, on the field, at chapel, and anywhere else we’re doing Life Together. Duties and Responsibilities Teach a full-time load of 24 load hours per academic year, with responsibility for undergraduate courses in special education and inclusive practices and the potential to teach additional courses in elementary and/or secondary education based on background and program needs. Opportunities to teach graduate courses may be available in the future. Design interactive and engaging classroom experiences that integrate faith and learning while modeling effective, evidence-based practices for supporting students with disabilities and other diverse learning needs in inclusive educational settings. Advise students on licensure requirements, degree progress, and professional development while coaching students in the professional and ethical practices expected of educators, including thoughtful and appropriate use of person-first and identity-first language. Supervise and mentor pre-service teachers through advising and field experiences. Collaborate with Education Department colleagues to strengthen teacher preparation programs including contributions to accreditation and program-review processes and support alignment with applicable state and national standards for educator preparation, particularly those related to special education and inclusive practice. Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with local schools, special education professionals, and other educational partners to strengthen clinical experiences and connections between university coursework and P–12 practice. Serve the university, community, and profession through committee work, partnerships with schools and community organizations, participation in faculty governance, and involvement in relevant professional organizations. Participate in professional development and continuing education to remain current with research, policy, legislation, and emerging practices in special education, inclusive education, and teacher preparation. Conduct scholarly research and/or engage in scholarly activity that contributes to special education, inclusive education, teacher preparation, or related areas. Possess excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Attend chapel and participate in the broader spiritual and community life of the university. Typical Qualifications Candidates must have a personal, vibrant faith and Christian walk and be strongly committed to the educational mission and evangelical Christian orientation of the University. Taylor University is a Christ-centered educational institution, and an evangelical, interdenominational covenant community committed to advancing life-long learning and ministering the redemptive love and truth of Jesus Christ to a world in need. Candidates will be expected to affirm the Taylor University Life Together Covenant, Statement of Faith, and essential documents. An earned doctorate in education or a related field is preferred. ABD and master’s-level candidates may be considered. Evidence of significant, effective instructional experience and a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching is essential. The candidate should have diverse teaching experiences and demonstrated expertise in special education, including knowledge of evidence-based practices for supporting students with disabilities in inclusive educational settings. Additionalteaching experience in the elementary or secondary classroomis preferred. The successful candidate will contribute to our dynamic teacher preparation program by preparing future elementary educators who are competent, caring, reflective, and prepared for world service. Supplemental Information The Education Department comprises eleven faculty and staff and is accredited by CAEP and the Indiana Department of Education. Undergraduate Teacher Education candidates may obtain licensure in All-grade (P-12) Art and Music Education, K-6 Elementary Education, and Secondary Education (grades 5-12) offered in Biology, Chemistry, English, English/Theatre Arts, Mathematics, Mathematics/Computer Science, Physics, Physics/Mathematics, Physical Science, Social Studies and Spanish. Additional licensure offerings include Mild and Intense Intervention and Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages. The Taylor University Education Department also offers Transition to Teaching and Online Licensure Programs ( https://www.taylor.edu/online/programs-licensures/transition-to-teaching ). Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Education Related Jobs Tenure-Track in Psychology Taylor University Upland, Indiana Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Open Rank Faculty Position, Tech and Human Flourishing LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Birmingham, Alabama Azusa, California Chicago, Illinois Wheaton, Illinois Longview, Texas Alabama Florida Grand Rapids, Michigan Michigan South Carolina Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Houston, Texas Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida California Pennsylvania Minnesota Iowa Charleston, South Carolina ORANGE CITY, Iowa Redding, California Texas Cedarville, Ohio St. Paul, Minnesota Illinois Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Simpson University Calvin University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Charleston Southern University Samford University Cedarville University Messiah University Wheaton College Palm Beach Atlantic University Moody Bible Institute Northwestern College Anderson University - SC Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Health Professions Executive Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Mathematics Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Accounting / Finance Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Education Faculty Careers - Business Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
