    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-in-psychology-upland-indiana-12682": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track in Psychology",
      "description": "Tenure-Track in Psychology in Upland, Indiana | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure-Track in Psychology Taylor University Upland, Indiana Share Save Job Apply for This Job Taylor University is seeking applications and nominations of distinctive candidates for a tenure-track position in Psychology beginning in February or August 2027. Rank and salary are dependent upon qualifications and experience. Mission and Commitment Taylor's mission is to develop servant-leaders marked with a passion to minister Christ’s redemptive love, grace, and truth to a world in need. As a community, Taylor faculty, staff, and students commit to living out Christ’s love and truth in the here and now. We worship together, serve one another, and grow in faith as we learn in the classroom, on the field, at chapel, and anywhere else we’re doing Life Together. Duties and Responsibilities Teaching will consist primarily of courses in the psychology major and will include upper-division courses in the candidate’s field of expertise.  The normal teaching load is 24 hours per academic year.  Scholarly activity, participation in professional activities or organizations, student advising, weekly office hours, faculty governance responsibilities, and chapel attendance are expected. Typical Qualifications A doctoral degree in psychology and the ability to mentor students in psychological research are expected. ABD candidates will be considered. Excellence in teaching is essential, including integration of faith into the classroom. The candidate should be able to teach a variety of undergraduate level psychology courses, ranging from introductory to advanced levels. Prior teaching experience is desirable. Successful candidates should have demonstrated abilities toward or a record of research and publication. Area of expertise is open, however, those with specialization in experimental psychology or neuroscience are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates must have a personal Christian faith and be strongly committed to the educational mission of the University. Taylor University is a Christ-centered educational institution, and an evangelical, interdenominational covenant community committed to advancing life-long learning and ministering the redemptive love and truth of Jesus Christ to a world in need. Candidates will be expected to affirm the Taylor University Life Together Covenant, Statement of Faith, and essential documents. Supplemental Information The Psychology Department at Taylor has seven full-time faculty members.  The department has close ties with kinesiology, social work, public health, pre-art therapy, and education departments. There are approximately 170 psychology majors, making psychology the largest single major on campus. In addition, the psychology department has over 140 students in the departmental minors: General Psychology, Autism Studies & Interventions, Counseling, Neuroscience, Industrial-Organizational, Health & Wellness, and Intercultural Psychology. The psychology programs have a practicum and/or directed research requirement which encourages student mentoring opportunities. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Psychology Related Jobs Psychological Sciences - Full-time Faculty Bethel University St. Paul, Minnesota Posted - September 24, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Jim and Sharon Harrod Chair of Christian Thought & Full-Time Tenure Track Position Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Open Rank Faculty Position, Tech and Human Flourishing LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Chicago, Illinois Grand Rapids, Michigan Iowa Alabama Birmingham, Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota Charleston, South Carolina Ohio Houston, Texas Anderson, South Carolina Longview, Texas Minnesota Florida Redding, California California South Carolina Pennsylvania Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Azusa, California Illinois West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Wheaton, Illinois Cedarville, Ohio Trending Companies Wheaton College Calvin University Palm Beach Atlantic University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Anderson University - SC Azusa Pacific University Simpson University Messiah University Samford University Moody Bible Institute Northwestern College Cedarville University Houston Christian University Charleston Southern University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Computer science Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Accounting / Finance NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Executive Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Religion Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Admini