    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-in-communication-professional-writing-upland-indiana-12679": {
      "title": "Tenure Track in Communication",
      "description": "Tenure Track in Communication - Professional Writing in Upland, Indiana | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure Track in Communication - Professional Writing Taylor University Upland, Indiana Share Save Job Apply for This Job The Department of Communication invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Professional Writing. The successful candidate will teach courses in the written side of communication – including but not limited to business writing, social media writing, freelance writing, editing, Microsoft 365 tools, technical writing, and capstone courses. Experience in book publishing processes is a plus. The candidate will also be called upon to assist the department in teaching the required core courses, advise and mentor undergraduate students, engage in scholarly research and general market writing, and provide meaningful service to the community, department, and university. Mission and Commitment Taylor's mission is to develop servant-leaders marked with a passion to minister Christ’s redemptive love, grace, and truth to a world in need. As a community, Taylor faculty, staff, and students commit to living out Christ’s love and truth in the here and now. We worship together, serve one another, and grow in faith as we learn in the classroom, on the field, at chapel, and anywhere else we’re doing Life Together. The Professional Writing program is rooted in the understanding that every organization needs communicators who are strong writers and editors. The classes in the major are designed to give students experience in the many types of writing that they may be called upon to do in a future job. While some students come in with a desire to write and publish their own books, and while they are encouraged to hone their skills toward book publication through classes that overview the publishing world and its processes, they are also encouraged to understand that God can use their love of and skill with words to become valuable employees. Duties and Responsibilities Testify to personal experience of salvation in Jesus Christ, affirm belief in the University’s Statement of Faith, abide by and practice our Life Together Covenant, and both personally agree with and support the Foundational Documents of Taylor University. Teach a four-course load per semester (total of 12 credit hours). Advise and mentor students, supporting academic, professional, and personal development. Conduct and publish scholarly research in the field of writing or communication, as well as publish articles and/or books for the general audience. Actively participate in departmental service, curriculum development, committee work, and faith integration. Serve as faculty adviser to the Taylor University Professional Writers Conference. Build and maintain strong connections with alumni, local nonprofits, and industry professionals to support internships, service-learning, article interview projects, and community partnerships. Promote student achievements, alumni success stories, and program highlights through digital and in-person engagement. Actively work with admissions for recruitment and advancement. Assist students in developing professional portfolios. Typical Qualifications An appropriately earned doctorate or MFA is preferred but consideration will be given to candidates in the midst of doctoral or MFA studies. Excellence in teaching and a demonstrated or emerging record of published writing. Commitment to collegiality, collaboration, service learning, and integration of faith and learning. Supplemental Information The Communication Department consists of six full-time faculty, and one full-time program assistant serving approximately 120 students in each of 4 majors: Professional Writing, Communication, Public Relations, and Multimedia Journalism. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Communication/ Design/ Media Related Jobs Tenure-Track in Elementary Education Taylor University Upland, Indiana Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure-Track in Literature Taylor University Upland, Indiana Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Jim and Sharon Harrod Chair of Christian Thought & Full-Time Tenure Track Position Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Posted - September 16, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Campus Ministry Director Assistant Professor Of Marketing Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Pennsylvania Wheaton, Illinois Ohio Redding, California Iowa Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania St. Paul, Minnesota Charleston, South Carolina Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Illinois West Palm Beach, Florida Minnesota California Grand Rapids, Michigan Florida Longview, Texas Houston, Texas Michigan South Carolina Birmingham, Alabama Cedarville, Ohio Chicago, Illinois Azusa, California Texas Trending Companies Messiah University Moody Bible Institute Northwestern College LeTourneau University Wheaton College Simpson University Palm Beach Atlantic University Azusa Pacific University Calvin University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Samford University Houston Christian University Anderson University - SC Cedarville University Charleston Southern University Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Psychology Facul