    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/psychological-sciences-full-time-faculty-st-paul-minnesota-12678": {
      "title": "Psychological Sciences",
      "description": "Psychological Sciences - Full-time Faculty in St. Paul, Minnesota | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Psychological Sciences - Full-time Faculty Bethel University St. Paul, Minnesota Share Save Job Apply for This Job Psychological Sciences - Full-time Faculty About the role - Full-time (24 credit load), tenure-track position in the Department of Psychological Sciences, including teaching, research, mentoring of undergraduate students, and service to the university. A clinical faculty appointment is also an option, with clinical work substituting for scholarly research. Courses are delivered predominantly face-to-face. What you'll do - Teach some combination of https://catalog.bethel.edu/academic-programs/college-of-arts-sciences-and-education/undergraduate-programs/psychological-sciences/psychological-sciences-bs/, and/or other courses in the specialty of the candidate. - Actively engage in either creating and implementing a research agenda; OR a clinical practice that engages your teaching. - Advise undergraduate students regarding their academic plans and career. - Mentor and advise student research projects or preparation for clinical professions. - Collaborate in departmental programming. - Serve on a university committee(s) as assigned. - Contribute to an academic environment that seeks to advance inclusive excellence in the department and the discipline. Qualifications Skills: - Ability to teach core Psychology courses, in addition to other courses that reflect the candidate's specialty or the needs of the department. - Ability to engage with and mentor students. - Ability to implement a research plan and commitment to involving students in research projects; OR sustained clinical practice that contributes to the field and enriches teaching. - Commitment to exploring connections between psychology and the Christian Faith. - Ability and desire to support inclusive excellence in the University community. - Demonstrated ability to collaborate and work effectively as a member of a team. Experience: - Teaching and research experience preferred Education: - Ph.D., Psy.D., or ABD in Psychology or related field required Additional Responsibilities: Bethel's mission is to educate and equip students to lead lives of impact through transformative academics in a Christ-centered community. Bethel's employee community plays a central role in developing our students as whole and holy persons. To carry out this mission, Bethel uses the foundation of our guiding documents, the Affirmation of Faith, Community Covenant, and Key Policies. Bethel expects all employees to actively participate in creating our Christ-centered community by agreeing with and abiding by our core beliefs in the Affirmation of Faith and supporting all other beliefs as Biblical, responsible, and thoughtful approaches while avoiding dissension and divisiveness. Employees teach and mentor students and help one another uphold our Community Covenant commitments. As a result of these expectations, all University employees act as ministers of the gospel of Jesus Christ by actively partnering with the University to carry out its mission and foster Bethel's Christ-centered covenant community. Other Duties: The essential functions, tasks and responsibilities of this position may change from time to time. Bethel University reserves the right to add or omit duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the University or its leadership. Additional tasks or duties required of the position, will be communicated to the incumbent with specificity to ensure the employee may perform their role with complete understanding. This job description is intended to describe the general level of work being performed; it is not intended to be all-inclusive. Remote Work and Sponsorship Restrictions: Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. This is an in-person position, so remote work is not an option for this role. Compensation We are open to hiring an Assistant, Associate or Full Professor for this position. The range for an Assistant Professor is $55,599 - $70,043, Associate Professor is $62,927 - $84,168 and Full Professor is $77,265 - $95,904. Salary and rank determined by education and experience. Benefits Bethel is committed to offering meaningful benefits to our employees including health insurance, retirement plans, and a generous time off package. Learn more about these offerings https://www.bethel.edu/employment/working/benefits Join a Christ-centered community committed to inclusive excellence, reconciliation, and flourishing for all. https://www.bethel.edu/employment/working/commitment-diversity-in-hiring Additional Information We will begin reviewing applications on October 15, 2026. Bethel University is a leader in Christ-centered higher education with approximately 4,700 students from 50 states and 32 countries enrolled in undergraduate, graduate, seminary, and adult education programs. Based in St. Paul, Minnesota, Bethel offers bachelor's and advanced degrees in nearly 100 fields. Educationally excellent classroom-based and online programs equip graduates to make exceptional contributions in life-long service to God and the world. Bethel University's Christ-centered mission includes a commitment to equal educational opportunity and equal employment opportunity. Bethel does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, national origin, sex, marital status, disability, status with regard to public assistance, familial status, or age in its admissions, educational programs, or employment practices. To apply, visit https://apptrkr.com/9851378 je-23ada065b7304ec6990b4549c269a925 Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Psychology Related Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Jim and Sharon Harrod Chair of Christian Thought & Full-Time Tenure Track Position Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Residence Life Educator Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Birmingham, Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Alabama South Carolina Illinois Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Grand Rapids, Michigan Michigan St. Paul, Minnesota Texas Minnesota Cedarville, Ohio Redding, California Chicago, Illinois Houston, Texas Pennsylvania Anderson, South Carolina Wheaton, Illinois Iowa Florida Longview, Texas Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida Charleston, South Carolina California Azusa, California Trending Companies Moody Bible Institute Charleston Southern University Northwestern College LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University Simpson University Anderson University - SC InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Palm Beach Atlantic University Calvin University Samford University Messiah University Wheaton College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Business NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Other Accounting / Finance Education Faculty Careers - Engineering Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Health Professions Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Mathematics Executive Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713 Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
