    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-electrical-engineering-shawnee-oklahoma-12677": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering in Shawnee, Oklahoma | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant or Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Oklahoma Baptist University Shawnee, Oklahoma Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 500 W University St, Shawnee, OK 74804, USA OBU Mission Statement OBU transforms lives by equipping students to pursue academic excellence, integrate faith with all areas of knowledge, engage a diverse world, and live worthy of the high calling of God in Christ. Expectations for all Employees Oklahoma Baptist University achieves its mission through a shared commitment to the following expectations. All employees must embrace these expectations and model them in their behavior. Demonstrate      commitment to the essentials of the Christian faith. Commit to the      mission and vision of Oklahoma Baptist University. Treat people with      dignity and respect. Build      relationships on honesty, integrity, and trust. Strive for      excellence through teamwork, leadership, and a strong work ethic. Manage human and      financial resources wisely and efficiently. Purpose: OBU is a distinguished Christian university committed to integrating faith and learning. We strive to provide an education that fosters intellectual growth, spiritual development, and a commitment to service. Our Engineering Department is dedicated to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and industry engagement. We are seeking an enthusiastic and experienced Electrical Engineering Professor to join our faculty. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in electrical engineering, significant industry experience, and a commitment to Christian values. This position involves teaching undergraduate courses, participating in scholarly activities, and mentoring students. Essential Functions: •\tTeach a variety of electrical engineering courses at the undergraduate level to include electrical circuits, controls, microprocessors, and power systems, depending on the applicant’s experience and expertise. •\tDevelop and implement innovative teaching methods that integrate faith and learning. •\tMentor and advise students on academic and career goals. •\tCollaborate with industry partners to enhance the practical learning experience for students. •\tContribute to departmental and university service activities such as ABET accreditation, curriculum and program development, and student recruitment. •\tRemain current in their field by participating in scholarly activities and being active in professional organizations. •\tUphold and promote the Christian mission and values of the university. Other Duties: •\tAssist with purchasing lab equipment. Required Qualifications: •\tM.S. in Electrical Engineering or a closely related field with engineering work experience. •\tStrong commitment to integrating Christian faith with academic excellence. •\tExcellent communication and people skills. •\tAbility to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. •\tActive involvement in a Christian church and alignment with the university’s statement of faith. Preferred Qualifications: •\tPh.D. in Electrical Engineering or a closely related field. •\tDemonstrated excellence in teaching. •\t5 or more years of industry experience in electrical engineering. •\tProfessional Engineering license. •\tExperience in curriculum development and academic program assessment. •\tInvolvement in professional engineering organizations. Physical Requirements: •\tMust be able to lift up to 50 lbs •\tMust be able to operate the field maintenance equipment Special Requirements: •\tMust be a member of a local evangelical* Christian church. *Evangelical is a broad term referring to segment within Christianity which maintains the authority of the Bible and the belief in salvation by faith in Jesus alone. •\tPlease apply using the link for “Faculty Applications” on the OBU website at: https://www.okbu.edu/hr/jobs.html OBU Benefits Summary: OBU understands that our employees are our most valuable assets when fulfilling our mission. We strive to offer an extensive array of benefits and opportunities for employees to choose from. Full-time employees benefit from the generous OBU provision of premium contributions for nationwide family-friendly Health and Dental coverages along with free life insurance that includes accidental death and dismemberment equal to an employee’s base salary. OBU provides access to optional employee-paid ancillary benefits like vision, hospitalization, critical illness, accident, additional employee-paid family life insurance coverages, and education benefits at OBU and other institutions of higher education. There is generous paid time off that includes annual granted vacation time, accrued sick leave, six annual holidays, and week-long breaks for Thanksgiving and Christmas that include energy conservation days. For all employees working at least half-time, there is an employer matching opportunity for retirement investments in a 403(b)(9) plan administered by Guide Stone. There are numerous other perks and opportunities for OBU employees including FREE family membership to the OBU Recreation and Wellness Center or RAWC, Global outreach university mission trips, cafeteria discounts, and parking privileges to name a few. For more information about the current OBU employee benefits and opportunities, please contact the Human Resources staff at [email protected] . Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Engineering Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General) Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations ORANGE CITY, Iowa Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Illinois Alabama Charleston, South Carolina Houston, Texas Chicago, Illinois Ohio Florida Iowa Texas South Carolina West Palm Beach, Florida Longview, Texas Azusa, California Wheaton, Illinois California Cedarville, Ohio Michigan Pennsylvania Grand Rapids, Michigan Birmingham, Alabama Redding, California Minnesota St. Paul, Minnesota Trending Companies Cedarville University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Calvin University Azusa Pacific University Samford University Houston Christian University Simpson University LeTourneau University Palm Beach Atlantic University Moody Bible Institute Northwestern College Charleston Southern University Anderson University - SC Messiah University Wheaton College Trending Categories NonProfit Careers Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-of-jewish-studies-chicago-illinois-12676": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Jewish Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Jewish Studies in Chicago, Illinois | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor of Jewish Studies Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 820 N La Salle Dr, Chicago, IL 60610, USA Location : Onsite, Chicago, IL Employment Type: Full-Time Annual Salary Range: $ 60,000 - 70,000 Start Date: January 2027 Department: Intercultural Studies Field, Undergraduate School The salary range above represents the anticipated hiring range for this position. Rank and salary are commensurate with academic credentials and experience. Final offers are determined based on a variety of factors including skills, experience, qualifications, internal equity, and other job-related considerations. To access a list of benefits for full-time jobs, click here . Are you passionate about combining biblical scholarship, teaching, and Jewish ministry to prepare the next generation of Christian leaders? Moody Bible Institute is seeking an engaging and dedicated scholar-practitioner to join our Undergraduate School as an Assistant Professor of Jewish Studies at our Chicago campus. This is a unique opportunity to bring your academic expertise, ministry experience, and creative vision into the classroom while mentoring students and contributing to the continued growth and development of our Jewish Studies program. If you are energized by rigorous scholarship, meaningful student formation, and the opportunity to help shape a program with lasting ministry impact, we invite you to consider joining the Moody community. About Us Moody Bible Institute is a Christ-centered higher education and media ministry dedicated to equipping people with the truth of God's Word. Through trusted biblical teaching, media, and educational resources, Moody reaches audiences around the world with the gospel and seeks to make a lasting Kingdom impact. The Opportunity As an Assistant Professor of Jewish Studies , you will combine teaching, scholarship, ministry experience, and student mentorship to contribute to Moody’s Christ-centered educational mission. The ideal candidate will be an engaging classroom teacher with an entrepreneurial mindset who brings creativity and initiative to the continued growth and enrichment of the Jewish Studies program. In addition to teaching, you will have opportunities to contribute to course and program development, collaborate across academic disciplines, mentor students in their academic and spiritual formation, and strengthen connections between Moody, the broader academic community, and faith-based ministry. What You’ll Do Prepare syllabi and teach undergraduate courses in Jewish Studies, including biblical, historical, and theological perspectives, as well as Messianic prophecy. Partner with the Program Head to establish appropriate course learning outcomes and assess student achievement. Teach effectively across multiple modalities, including in-person and online instruction using learning management systems. Serve as an academic advisor and mentor to assigned students, supporting both academic progress and spiritual development. Maintain a regular on-campus presence and scheduled office hours in accordance with faculty guidelines. Participate actively in field, committee, and faculty meetings. Collaborate with faculty and academic leadership to identify opportunities for program growth, scholarly engagement, course development, and community outreach. Contribute to the academic vitality and broader impact of Jewish Studies within Moody and the wider academic and faith community. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Master's degree in a relevant academic field. Current or demonstrated engagement in Jewish ministry. Ability to teach cross-departmentally in areas such as biblical studies, theology, evangelism, intercultural studies, or applied theology. Commitment to transformational learning and the holistic development of students. Ability and willingness to teach in multiple instructional modalities. Desire for continued spiritual growth and a commitment to mentoring students. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated personal integrity, passion, perseverance, and professionalism. Collaborative and team-oriented approach, with openness to varied ministry perspectives and approaches. Understanding of and commitment to the authority of Scripture and Moody's mission. Legal authorization to work in the United States without employer sponsorship. Preferred Doctorate in related discipline. Demonstrated experience developing or leading new academic initiatives, programs, or scholarly activities that foster program growth, student engagement, and broader institutional impact. Work Environment This position is based at Moody Bible Institute’s Chicago campus and requires a regular on-campus presence. Faculty responsibilities include classroom instruction, academic advising and mentoring, scholarship, committee participation, and service within a collaborative, Christ-centered academic community. Work is primarily performed in professional office and classroom settings, with opportunities for ministry-related engagement. Instruction is primarily in person, with faculty expected to effectively utilize virtual teaching and learning technologies as needed. Faculty schedules generally fall Monday through Friday, with occasional evening and weekend responsibilities based on academic and institutional needs. Additional Information Candidates must demonstrate alignment with Moody Bible Institute's mission, doctrinal beliefs, and Christian values. Employees are required to affirm Moody's Statement of Faith and adhere to Community Standards. Moody Bible Institute values diversity and seeks team members who engage others in ways that honor its biblical foundation. Moody complies with applicable nondiscrimination laws and, as a religious institution, requires employees to hold beliefs consistent with its Doctrinal Statement and Community Standards. Why Join Us? Bring Your Calling to Moody . Your scholarship, ministry experience, and investment in students can have an impact far beyond the classroom. At Moody, you will have the opportunity to help students grow in knowledge, faith, and preparation for ministry while contributing to the future of our Jewish Studies program. If you are ready to bring your passion for teaching and ministry to a community committed to biblical truth and preparing the next generation of Christian leaders, we invite you to apply and explore what your next chapter could look like at Moody. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Religion Salary: $60,000.00 - $70,000.00 Commensurate with Experience Education: Master's Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Studies LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 14, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Finance Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Trending Locations ORANGE CITY, Iowa Illinois Chicago, Illinois Houston, Texas Azusa, California South Carolina California Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Texas Minnesota Charleston, South Carolina Anderson, South Carolina Ohio Longview, Texas Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota Pennsylvania Redding, California West Palm Beach, Florida Grand Rapids, Michigan Cedarville, Ohio Wheaton, Illinois Florida Michigan Birmingham, Alabama Iowa Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University Northwestern College Azusa Pacific University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Wheaton College Cedarville University Charleston Southern University Houston Christian University Moody Bible Institute Simpson University LeTourneau University Calvin University Messiah University Samford University Anderson University - SC Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Engineering Education Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Executive Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Psychology Accounting / Finance Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Computer science Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
