    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/director-of-human-resources-olathe-kansas-12674": {
      "title": "Director of Human Resources",
      "description": "Director of Human Resources in Olathe, Kansas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Director of Human Resources MidAmerica Nazarene University Olathe, Kansas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Job Summary : Under the direction of the Vice President for Finance, plan, organize and oversee the university human resources management functions, including employee relations, strategic planning, legal compliance, compensation administration, payroll, HRIS, and faculty and staff planning and development. This position is a resource for all levels of the organization regarding employment, compensation, employee performance, benefits and other employee related issues. In addition, this position acts as liaison for university Risk Management issues with the carrier and various departments on campus. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: HR Related Duties and Responsibilities Plan, organize and oversee the university human resources management functions, including employee relations, strategic planning, legal compliance, compensation administration, HRIS and faculty and staff planning and development. Plan, coordinate and assist with employee relations and training activities; provide information to applicants and employees with human resources questions; conduct investigations related to human resources issues as appropriate. Identify issues and recommend improvements for effective Human Resources functions including benefit renewal, plan design changes, Employee Handbook and university policies and procedures. Plan, organize and implement compensation administration practices and procedures. This includes monitoring, setting and changing pay ranges for staff personnel, running reports for annual budget process, and coordinating pay increases/promotions. Develop, organize and implement performance management process. Administer and oversee recruitment process. An active member of the Diversity Advisory Committee (DAC). Plan, coordinate and oversee activities related to benefits administration. Such as: benefit renewal, coordinate with providers for problem resolution, and disseminate changes to the campus personnel. Plans, organizes and implements events connected to employee recognition, benefit enrollment and wellness activities, as well as Administrative Staff Assembly meetings (ASA). Works with the Faculty and Staff development director regarding training opportunities for staff. This includes being a member of the Faculty Welfare Committee. Manages Communication staff (the University Receptionist) to ensure that the university phone and reception area runs efficiently and effectively. Responsible to maintaining HR and Communication annual budget and expenses. Manage HR and communication staff. Explores all opportunities to maintain budgeted funds and cost saving initiatives in benefits, staffing and other areas within this position’s span of control. Payroll Related Duties and Responsibilities Manage payroll staff to ensure proper payment process and all legal compliance of payroll payments for all University employees. Audits reports (maintains compliance) on federal withholding, state withholding, unemployment compensation as well as payroll edits each pay period. Facilitates improvements in payroll operations/functions by assisting in the development and maintenance of computer systems used in payroll operations. Completes salary survey information as needed and annually for the Integrated Postsecondary Education System (IPEDS). Ensures that MNU is collecting deductions from employees accurately and processes the invoices for benefit carriers and other vendor payments in a timely manner. Risk Management Duties and Responsibilities Liaison for university Risk Management issues with the carrier and coordinates renewal reporting and processes with the VP for Finance. Works with other departments regarding Risk Management issues such as Facility Services. Reports liability claims to the carrier and works with departments with required areas of improvement. Serves on the Emergency Operations Plan (EOP) committee. Coordinates and reports worker compensation claims with the injured party and the carrier. Oversees approval and education for those employees, including students, that drive MNU vehicles and equipment. Qualifications Qualifications/Skills Required: General understanding of basic accounting and payroll processing. Demonstrated and proven ability in the understanding/knowledge of all legal requirements for payroll and Human Resources compliance. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to relate to a diverse clientele and all levels within MNU. Detailed oriented with strong attention to detail with the ability to problem solve effectively and quickly. Ability to be personally supportive of the Christian character and mission of the University to encourage and sustain mission-fit personnel recruiting. Solid computer skills including Microsoft Office Products. Excellent listening and analytical skills to manage and guide others through conflict resolution and management. This includes skills to discern when issues can be resolved or when they need to be moved to a higher level. Education and/or Experience: Bachelor’s required; Master’s degree preferred. Minimum of 5 years of demonstrated ability and experience in payroll and Human Resources, 3 years of experience in higher education is preferred. Experience using payroll software and ability to understand/adapt to various computer software programs. Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Human Resources Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Director of Graduate Teacher Education Oklahoma Baptist University Shawnee, Oklahoma (Hybrid) Posted - September 21, 2026 View Deputy Title IX Coordinator PT Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant Director, Financial Aid and Scholarships Anderson University - SC Anderson, South Carolina Posted - August 28, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Pennsylvania Texas Wheaton, Illinois Longview, Texas Ohio Anderson, South Carolina Alabama California Birmingham, Alabama Cedarville, Ohio Minnesota Michigan West Palm Beach, Florida Illinois Charleston, South Carolina Azusa, California Iowa St. Paul, Minnesota Florida Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Redding, California Grand Rapids, Michigan ORANGE CITY, Iowa Houston, Texas South Carolina Chicago, Illinois Trending Companies Moody Bible Institute Anderson University - SC Charleston Southern University Simpson University Cedarville University Messiah University Northwestern College Calvin University Wheaton College InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Azusa Pacific University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Education Executive Faculty Careers - Other Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Health Professions Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Religion Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
