    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/program-development-specialist-study-abroad-advisor-wheaton-illinois-12673": {
      "title": "Program Development Specialist/Study Abroad Advisor",
      "description": "Program Development Specialist/Study Abroad Advisor in Wheaton, Illinois | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Program Development Specialist/Study Abroad Advisor Wheaton College Wheaton, Illinois Share Save Job Apply for This Job Program Development Specialist/Study Abroad Advisor Global Programs and Studies Job Overview The Program Development Specialist and Study Abroad Advisor provides program-related support for Wheaton-run semester programs and international internships; advises and assists students during application and preparation for off-campus study or international experiences; and works in tandem with academic and campus offices to facilitate student participation in international programs. The Program Development Specialist and Study Abroad Advisor reports directly to the Executive Director of Global Programs and Studies. This is an exempt position; 40 hours/week, 12 months/year, that pays between $53,000 - $55,000. Requires occasional evening responsibilities as well as occasional travel. Duties and Responsibilities Manage the operational aspects, administrative planning, communication, and marketing/promotion for Wheaton faculty-led semester programs, building and maintaining relationships with vendors and third-party program provider(s) to support programs. Develop program budgets and monitor program revenue and expenses. Facilitate payment of program expenses, including electronic payment disbursements to students. Advise students for Wheaton-in semester study abroad opportunities in light of their curricular goals, intercultural interests, and program offerings. Provide support from application and pre-departure through return. Facilitate College application and registration processes for non-Wheaton student participation on a Wheaton faculty-led program. Develop relationships with the global education offices at other CCCU campuses to market/promote participation in Wheaton faculty-led programs. Partner with the Executive Director and academic departments to identify areas of growth and opportunities for additional faculty-led programs and collaborate in all aspects of program development from program proposal to program delivery. Provide support for independent student travel registration (international internship/field experience and international student teachers), explaining processes and College-wide requirements. Lead, coordinate, and manage budget for one annually assigned GPS event and support all planned GPS events (e.g., Study Abroad Fair, bi-annual GPS Photo Contest, GPS sessions at Admissions events, New Student Orientation, and other events). Liaise with campus offices (e.g., Admissions, Academic Advising, Registrar’s Office, SFS, SHS, Student Wellness, Housing, Risk Management, etc.) to assist students planning education abroad experiences and, as necessary, to support processes associated with new program development. Build and maintain GoGlobal/TerraDotta applications and system workflows in supported travel areas; Maintain GPS Wheaton-in semester study abroad program pages on the Wheaton website using College CMS. Conduct weekly academic eligibility reviews of all fall and spring students registered in GoGlobal. Represent and participate in various campus committees and projects related to the GPS office such as the GPS Advisory Committee. Advise students for Approved Partner programs, both summer and semester, as needed. This job description is intended to represent key areas of responsibility; specific assignments may vary from time to time, and other duties may be assigned. Professional Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Three years of related job experience Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to synthesize information clearly Strong organization and program management/administration skills Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite Experience working with a web content management system (CMS), student information system (SIS) and/or client relationship management system (CRM) Excellent time management skills with the ability to strategically prioritize tasks Demonstrated ability to work as an effective team member Professional Preferred Qualifications Cross-cultural or international study experience Experience working in a higher education office Faith Qualifications Affirmation of the Wheaton College Statement of Faith as a faithful expression of one’s own theological convictions Affirmation of the biblical standards for Christian character and God-honoring behavior described throughout the Wheaton College Community Covenant, and promise to adhere to them in personal practice Support of the Wheaton College Christ-Centered Diversity Commitment, the Gender Equity Vision Statement, and the College’s Convictions on Human Sexuality.  These commitments can be found on the Wheaton College website. Physical Requirements The employee is regularly required to sit, talk, or hear; frequently required to use repetitive hand motion, handle or feel, and to stand, walk, reach, bend or lift up to 10 pounds. FLSA Status – Exempt Updated - September 2026 Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Salary: $53,000 - $55,000 Per Year Education: Bachelor's Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Transfer Evaluation Analyst Wheaton College Wheaton, Illinois Posted - September 1, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Finance Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Florida Michigan Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania South Carolina Minnesota Illinois Alabama Cedarville, Ohio Pennsylvania California St. Paul, Minnesota Chicago, Illinois Houston, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida Ohio Azusa, California Grand Rapids, Michigan Wheaton, Illinois Charleston, South Carolina Birmingham, Alabama Texas Redding, California Longview, Texas Anderson, South Carolina Iowa ORANGE CITY, Iowa Trending Companies Houston Christian University Messiah University Simpson University Moody Bible Institute Calvin University Azusa Pacific University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Anderson University - SC Northwestern College Wheaton College Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University Charleston Southern University LeTourneau University Cedarville University Trending Categories Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Engineering Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Mathematics Executive Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Computer science NonProfit Careers Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
