    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/new-testament-faculty-bethany-oklahoma-12672": {
      "title": "New Testament Faculty in Bethany, Oklahoma",
      "description": "New Testament Faculty in Bethany, Oklahoma | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job New Testament Faculty Southern Nazarene University Bethany, Oklahoma Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 6729 NW 39th Expy, Bethany, OK 73008, USA Overview Position Type: Faculty Full-Time Education Level: Terminal Degree Travel Percentage: Up to 25% Description: Full Time / Salary / Exempt WORK SITE Onsite Bethany JOB SUMMARY The School of Theology and Ministry seeks a full-time professor in New Testament on the Bethany, Oklahoma main campus. Rank based on previous experience and qualifications. The ideal candidate will be able to work collaboratively within the department and with other disciplines across campus.  They will be an energetic teacher who is able to innovate in the classroom and spark curiosity in the minds of traditional undergraduate students, both among our majors and across the student population in General Education courses.  The successful candidate will be firmly committed to the Wesleyan-Holiness theological tradition and its faithful expression in belief and practice. For more information about SNU, see our website: www.snu.edu RESPONSIBILITIES Essential Functions: Establish and maintain relationships with students to exemplify the motto “Character, Culture, Christ” as well as fulfill SNU’s mission to make Christ-like disciples in higher education. Teach 12 hours per semester in the areas of New Testament Greek, New Testament exegesis, and General Education for the department. Advise and mentor students with majors in the School of Theology and Ministry. Participate in the spiritual life of the SNU campus. Assist with assessment for School of Theology and Ministry programs and General Education courses taught in the department. Ability to engage in critical thinking. Ability to spark interest and curiosity in traditional undergraduate students. Ability to collaborate with other faculty and staff, and maintain collegial relations. Highly relational. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Southern Nazarene University is an expression of the Church of the Nazarene. According to SNU policy, all faculty and staff must profess faith in Jesus Christ, possess a strong personal Christian commitment and be committed to the SNU mission to make Christlike disciples through higher education in a Christ centered community. As an institution of the Church of the Nazarene, applicants must understand and embrace the biblical principle that all people are created in the image of God and should be treated with dignity and respect, including a belief in equal opportunity to work, contribute, and flourish without discrimination. Earned doctorate in New Testament from an accredited institution.  ABD candidates may also be considered. Commitment to the Wesleyan theological tradition. Membership in the Church of the Nazarene. Commitment to the preparation of both women and men for ministry. Preferred Qualifications: Completed doctorate Prior successful teaching experience at the undergraduate level in face-to-face setting Experience in contexts of diversity in research, scholarship and teaching Ordination in the Church of the Nazarene Supervision Received: Receives supervision and course assignments from the Chair of the School of Theology and Ministry. Supervision Exercised: N/A Application Process Candidates wishing to apply for this position will submit the following when given the opportunity to upload documents to our online application: A letter of application Curriculum vita with copies of academic transcripts (as a single document) In addition, the following documents will be submitted to the Search Committee at: jfitzgerald@snu.edu A one- to two-page statement of faith A two-page statement highlighting the candidate’s perspective and understanding with regard to the integration of Christian faith and learning Three letters of reference will be requested from candidates who are invited for an interview. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026 and priority will be given to applications submitted by October 15, 2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Job Information Job Category: Education Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Old Testament Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - August 10, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Finance Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Campus Ministry Director Assistant Professor Of Marketing Trending Locations Grand Rapids, Michigan Ohio Anderson, South Carolina Charleston, South Carolina Alabama Chicago, Illinois Longview, Texas Minnesota Florida Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Redding, California California St. Paul, Minnesota Pennsylvania South Carolina Michigan Azusa, California Wheaton, Illinois Cedarville, Ohio Iowa Birmingham, Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Illinois Houston, Texas Trending Companies Messiah University Moody Bible Institute Wheaton College Samford University Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University Palm Beach Atlantic University Charleston Southern University Houston Christian University Calvin University Anderson University - SC Northwestern College LeTourneau University Simpson University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Trending Categories Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Other Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Computer science NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713 Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
