    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-music-voice-st-paul-minnesota-12671": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Music: Voice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Music: Voice in St. Paul, Minnesota | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor, Music: Voice University of Northwestern - St. Paul St. Paul, Minnesota Share Save Job Apply for This Job Assistant Professor, Music: Voice VP Area: VP for Academic Affairs Department: School of Arts & Humanities Position Compensation: $58,956 - $61,400 Location: University Campus - St. Paul, Minnesota Who We Are: Northwestern is a faith-driven community, UNWavering in our Christ-centered principles and identity as those who profess faith in Jesus. Rooted in the unshakable foundation of God's Word and our calling to impact His world, our mission and vision flow from these core values, expressed through Christ-centered higher education at the University of Northwestern – St. Paul and through gospel outreach and faithfulness with Northwestern Media. Position Summary: This position provides excellence in teaching by advancing Northwestern's mission and strategic goals through undergraduate instruction in the Department of Music & Theatre. Responsibilities include coordinating vocal studies and teaching applied voice and related coursework, student advising, and supervision of senior projects and degree recitals to promote student success and career readiness. The role also contributes to recruitment and retention efforts and curriculum design, integrates technology into instruction, participates in service activities, and maintains professional expertise through ongoing development. Target Start: Fall 2027, with potential flexibility for an earlier start. Application Timeline: Position Open Until Filled. For priority consideration, please apply by January 8, 2027. Applications will be reviewed as received, and initial virtual screening interviews may occur prior to January. Campus interviews for selected finalists will be scheduled after January 8, 2027. Key Responsibilities: Every faculty member at University of Northwestern – St. Paul, has four governing job responsibilities: teaching with effective pedagogy, serving the university through committee work and community involvement, engaging in scholarship that demonstrates discipline-specific contributions beyond UNW, and classroom faith integration. These provide the framework for the following key responsibilities. · Teach a range of undergraduate courses integrating faith and learning across all assigned instructional formats. Includes planning and preparing courses with clearly articulated syllabi, effective use of the learning management system, and appropriate assessment, grading, and evaluation of student learning. Courses may include private voice lessons, vocal pedagogy, diction for singers, opera workshop, musical theatre workshop, and/or other areas of expertise and departmental need. · Provide leadership and coordination for the vocal area, including adjunct voice faculty and the Collaborative Piano Coordinator; oversee auditions, juries, and music scholarships; and collaborate with choral and theatre programs. · Contribute to curriculum design, course development, and assessment efforts in support of continuous program improvement and alignment across department degrees. · Advise and mentor assigned students, supporting their academic progress, career readiness, and professional development, including supervision of internships and experiential learning as appropriate. · Engage in ongoing professional development and scholarly or practitioner activity to remain current in applied discipline and effective postsecondary teaching practices. · Collaborate with department leadership to build and sustain relationships with off-campus partners to support internships, mentorships, and employment opportunities for students. · Contribute to the academic community through service on department and university committees, participation in student recruitment and retention initiatives, and support of institutional events and priorities. · Perform other duties as requested or assigned. Because our community is a significant part of our mission and the development of our students, all employees act as ministers of the gospel of Jesus Christ by actively partnering with the University to disciple students in growing intellectually and spiritually, and with Northwestern Media to lead people to Christ and nurture believers to mature in their faith. Qualifications: Required: • Terminal degree in vocal performance, vocal pedagogy, or a closely related music field. ABD and Artist Diploma will receive consideration. • Demonstrated professional activity in the community • Desire to engage in performance and/or scholarship, including the integration of profession and Christianity • Maintain a growing, personal relationship with Jesus Christ, reflect His character in all interactions, and faithfully uphold and embrace Northwestern's mission, Doctrinal Statement and Declaration of Christian Community Nice to Have: • Previous teaching at the post-secondary level • Expertise in both opera and musical theatre Key Skills: • Independent & Teamwork: Capable of working both independently and collaboratively, with minimal supervision. • Confidentiality: Maintains discretion and handles sensitive information appropriately. • Organizational Skills: Strong time management and problem-solving abilities; able to prioritize and meet deadlines with attention to detail. • Technical Proficiency: Intermediate to advanced computer skills, including Microsoft Office and related software. • Written & Verbal Communication: Strong writing, editing, proofreading, and verbal communication skills. • Flexibility: Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. • Background Check: Must pass initial and ongoing background checks as a condition of employment. Work Environment: The work environment involves working for a suburban, Christian university or Christian owned and operated radio station alongside those with a demonstrated commitment and personal relationship with Jesus Christ, a commitment to the mission and values of Northwestern, and an agreement to abide by all Northwestern policies. All applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. https://www.unwsp.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Benefits-Overview-12.18.25.pdf To apply, visit: https://jobs.unwsp.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-music-voice-minnesota-united-states je-563055d35b204255b370a68f494cde50 Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Related Jobs Open Rank Faculty Position, Tech and Human Flourishing LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Dean, School of Ministry Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - September 16, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Illinois Cedarville, Ohio Chicago, Illinois California Grand Rapids, Michigan Azusa, California Wheaton, Illinois Charleston, South Carolina ORANGE CITY, Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Florida Pennsylvania Michigan Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Redding, California St. Paul, Minnesota Iowa Minnesota Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama Texas Anderson, South Carolina Ohio South Carolina Alabama Houston, Texas Trending Companies Anderson University - SC Wheaton College Moody Bible Institute Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Calvin University Charleston Southern University Northwestern College Simpson University Samford University Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University Messiah University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA LeTourneau University Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Computer science NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Education Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our