    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/computer-science-faculty-position-point-lookout-missouri-12669": {
      "title": "Computer Science Faculty Position",
      "description": "Computer Science Faculty Position in Point Lookout, Missouri | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Computer Science Faculty Position College of the Ozarks Point Lookout, Missouri Share Save Job Apply for This Job College of the Ozarks invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Computer Science beginning in the Fall 2027 semester , though starting Spring 2027 may be possible. We seek a student-centered, self-motivated, and versatile faculty member with strong teaching skills and a demonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues. This position will focus primarily on the continued development and stewardship of our new Data Science and Artificial Intelligence program. The Computer Science Department offers majors and minors in Computer Information Science, Computer Science, and Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, as well as a minor in Cybersecurity and a range of general education courses. Teaching responsibilities will include both lower- and upper-division courses in Computer Science, Data Science, and Artificial Intelligence. The successful candidate will also be expected to maintain and develop course content and curriculum to ensure high-quality instruction and ongoing alignment with academic standards and industry needs. The standard teaching load is 24 credit hours over a nine-month academic year. College of the Ozarks is a distinctive liberal arts, work-study college of approximately 1,450 students, located in southwest Missouri near Branson. Deeply rooted in Christian faith and service, the College is known for its close-knit community, strong mentoring culture, and commitment to developing students academically, professionally, and spiritually. Class sizes are intentionally small, typically 10 to 25 students in STEM courses, allowing faculty to build meaningful relationships with students. College of the Ozarks seeks faculty members who embrace the institution’s Christian mission, demonstrate excellence in undergraduate teaching, serve as mentors and positive role models for students, and contribute collaboratively to the life of the College. Applicants should hold an M.S., D.Sc., or Ph.D. in Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related computing field. Candidates with degrees in a related discipline should also demonstrate substantial, well-documented experience in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence. To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, transcripts, and three letters of recommendation, including one from your pastor, to Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, Point Lookout, MO 65726, or by email to [email protected] . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Computer science Education: Master's Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Computer Science Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 9, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty, Artificial Intelligence & Analytics Indiana Wesleyan University Remote Posted - July 28, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Campus Ministry Director Assistant Professor Of Marketing Trending Locations Alabama Michigan Illinois Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama Ohio Chicago, Illinois Minnesota Grand Rapids, Michigan Cedarville, Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania St. Paul, Minnesota Texas California Houston, Texas Pennsylvania ORANGE CITY, Iowa South Carolina Iowa Redding, California Azusa, California Florida Wheaton, Illinois Charleston, South Carolina Trending Companies Anderson University - SC Moody Bible Institute Samford University Messiah University Wheaton College Northwestern College Houston Christian University Azusa Pacific University Cedarville University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Palm Beach Atlantic University Charleston Southern University Simpson University LeTourneau University Calvin University Trending Categories Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Computer science Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Mathematics Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty 