    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-tenured-full-time-philosophy-faculty-mishawaka-indiana-12668": {
      "title": "Tenure Track/Tenured Full Time Philosophy Faculty",
      "description": "Tenure Track/Tenured Full Time Philosophy Faculty in Mishawaka, Indiana | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure Track/Tenured Full Time Philosophy Faculty Bethel University - IN Mishawaka, Indiana Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 1001 Bethel Cir, Mishawaka, IN 46545, USA The Department of Religion and Philosophy at Bethel University (IN) is seeking applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty member in Philosophy starting August 2027. This position requires a full-time physical presence on campus in Mishawaka, Indiana. The Religion and Philosophy Department features programs in Philosophy, Christian Ministries (with concentrations in Biblical Studies, Children’s Ministry, Christian Ministries, Sports Ministry, and Youth Ministry), Intercultural Studies, Pastoral Ministries (BA/MA), and Worship Arts. The successful candidate will teach and develop coursework in Philosophy in response to departmental needs and his/her area(s) of expertise, and also teach courses in a complementary discipline such as ministry, biblical studies, literature, etc. The candidate is expected to engage in professional service and scholarly activities. Ideal candidates will demonstrate teaching excellence, exhibit enthusiastic interest in mentoring students, possess an interest in working collaboratively in the Christian liberal arts setting, demonstrate interest or experience in working with honors programs. Normal faculty duties include 12 hours of undergraduate teaching per semester as well as departmental and professional responsibilities (including program assessment). The preferred candidate would have a Ph.D. in Philosophy and demonstrated competency to teach in a complementary discipline. All interested candidates are invited to submit a cover letter, a current curriculum vita, and a statement of educational philosophy. As a Christian liberal arts institution, Bethel University desires that its faculty possess a vibrant Christian faith and an understanding of how that faith integrates with their discipline. Therefore, candidates are also required to submit a brief statement of faith and a statement on the integration of faith and learning. Bethel University is a Christian Liberal Arts institution affiliated with the Missionary Church. Faculty in the Department of Religion and Philosophy are required to affirm annually the following: 1. the Articles of Faith and Practice of the Missionary Church, ( https://mcusa.org/constitutionaldocs ), and 2. faithful membership/involvement in a local church that is aligned with Bethel’s statement of faith and lifestyle expectations. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Philosophy Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Jim and Sharon Harrod Chair of Christian Thought & Full-Time Tenure Track Position Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Open Rank Faculty Position, Tech and Human Flourishing LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor in Healthcare Management and Leadership Montreat College Montreat, North Carolina Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 3, 2026 View Associate Professor of Communication Regent University Virginia Beach, Virginia Posted - August 28, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Assistant Professor Of Marketing Associate Professor of Finance Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Texas West Palm Beach, Florida Michigan Chicago, Illinois Cedarville, Ohio St. Paul, Mi