    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/director-of-library-services-redding-california-12664": {
      "title": "Director of Library Services",
      "description": "Director of Library Services in Redding, California | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Director of Library Services Simpson University Redding, California Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2211 College View Dr, Redding, CA 96003, USA The Director of Library Services, as the chief administrative officer of the library and administrator with faculty status, provides vision and leadership in integrating new information technologies and expanding the library’s role as a Learning Commons in the university community; oversees all library operations; and, represents the university at meetings of professional library organizations.  Administrative faculty responsibilities continue through twelve months each year. Qualifications: 1.\tAn ALA-accredited graduate degree in library and information science 2.\tFive years of professional experience in academic librarianship 3.\tThree years management/supervisory experience 4.\tUnderstanding of and experience with Integrated Library Systems (ILS) 5.\tKnowledge of electronic resources employed by libraries 6.\tAptitude with productivity software 7.\tExperience with electronic resource licensing including utilization of consortium agreements and direct connections with vendors 8.\tExperience with assessment efforts and accreditation guidelines specific to libraries 9.\tThe ability to work harmoniously with faculty, staff and administration 10.\tA strong commitment to the university’s mission Preferred Qualifications: 1.\tA second graduate degree either in administration or in a subject area of importance to the university curriculum 2.\tExperience working with the various functions of a Learning Commons including writing and tutoring centers. 3.\tExperience with the OCLC WorldShare ILS 4.\tExperience with Microsoft Office 5.\tExperience with library content management systems (LibGuides preferred), integrated institutional database applications and learning management systems General Expectations : 1.\tPersonal relationship with Jesus, a vibrant Christian faith, and a commitment to Christian community; capable of sharing faith and engaging in conversations about Christ 2.\tDemonstrate Simpson University Values in the performance of all duties. 3.\tMaintain lifestyle in accordance with Simpson University Lifestyle Policy in Staff Handbook 4.\tMaintain the confidentiality of information, data and records 5.\tProperly exercise tact, diplomacy, discretion, and professional judgment 6.\tDemonstrate strong customer service skills in the performance of job duties 7.\tDemonstrate good organizational and communication skills in the performance of job duties 8.\tSupervises employees in accordance with Simpson University policies and procedures 9.\tSupport the overflow needs of other departments within the respective university area 10.\tPerform other duties in accordance with this position as deemed necessary by the immediate supervisor Responsibilities: 1.\tServes as the chief administrative officer of the library 2.\tProvides visionary leadership of library operations to align the library’s services and design with the current and future needs of the institution. 3.\tParticipates in faculty meetings and serves on faculty committees as appointed by the Provost 4.\tServes as a member of the Learning Resources Committee, Traditional Undergraduate Academic Council, Provost’s Council, and the Graduate Academic Council 5.\tOversees the development and application of policies governing the use, preservation and circulation of library collections 6.\tRecruits, leads, develops and evaluates a staff of professional librarians, paraprofessional employees and/or student employees 7.\tPromotes appropriate technologies in providing library services to faculty, students and staff that help foster a learning environment 8.\tPromotes information literacy and life-long learning through an effective library instructional program 9.\tWorks closely with the faculty and the Assistant Dean of Student Success to identify and provide the library services and resources necessary to support the university curriculum, faculty research, and student learning. 10.\tCreates and maintains a means of communication with faculty and students to keep them abreast of changes and new developments in the library 11.\tPrepares and manages the library’s budget 12.\tOversees collection development with an emphasis on electronic resources and the periodic review and revision of collection development policies 13.\tPrepares periodic library reports for administrators and committees of the university, government agencies and professional associations 14.\tMonitors the library’s compliance with the standards of the Association of College and Research Libraries and the university’s accrediting agencies 15.\tBuilds relationships with other libraries, networks and consortia for the common good Physical Requirements: Job   Title: Director   of Library Services Typical   Working Conditions: (Describe environment including exposure to heat, cold, fumes, chemicals,   allergens, mold, etc.) Indoors   in controlled environment Equipment   Used: (List all manual and automated equipment used in the course of performing   essential functions.) Computer,   scanner, copier, mouse, keyboard, camera, phone, stapler, 3-hole punch,   letter opener Essential   Physical Tasks: (List all physical tasks encountered in performing essential functions - i.e.   sitting for long periods of time using a computer, standing, climbing   ladders, etc.) Sitting   for long periods of time using a computer Lifting   individual items and boxed materials and carrying them from one place to   another Analysis of Physical Demands to Perform Essential Functions: Key (Based on typical week): N=Never R=Rarely (Les