    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/associate-provost-dean-of-arts-and-sciences-redding-california-12663": {
      "title": "Associate Provost/Dean of Arts and Sciences",
      "description": "Associate Provost/Dean of Arts and Sciences in Redding, California | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Associate Provost/Dean of Arts and Sciences Simpson University Redding, California Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2211 College View Dr, Redding, CA 96003, USA This position advances the university vision, mission, and strategic plan in relation to academic affairs activities leadership, and support for academic policy and procedure development and implementation for the traditional undergraduate program (College of Arts & Sciences), provides direction and oversight for segments of the academic area, and provides support for the Provost in all academic areas. Qualifications: 1.\tTerminal degree in an appropriate discipline. 2.\tMinimum 3-5 years as a Department Chair or equivalent academic leadership 3.\tMinimum of 5 years fulltime college level teaching experience 4.\tAppointment at the level of Associate Professor or Professor 5.\tSkilled at facilitating communication across different university areas 6.\tDemonstrated team building and team leadership ability 7.\tBudget experience within higher education context 8.\tExperience in college/university/department/program accreditation and assessment General Expectations: 1.\tPersonal relationship with Jesus, a vibrant Christian faith, and a commitment to Christian community; capable of sharing faith and engaging in conversations about Christ 2.\tDemonstrate Simpson University Values in the performance of all duties 3.\tMaintain lifestyle in accordance with Simpson University Lifestyle Policy in Staff Handbook 4.\tMaintain the confidentiality of information, data and records 5.\tProperly exercise tact, diplomacy, discretion, and professional judgment 6.\tDemonstrate strong customer service skills in the performance of job duties 7.\tDemonstrate good organizational and communication skills in the performance of job duties 8.\tSupervises employees in accordance with Simpson University policies and procedures 9.\tSupport the overflow needs of other departments within the respective university area 10.\tPerform other duties in accordance with this position as deemed necessary by the immediate supervisor Essential Functions: 1.\tChampion the objectives and interests for the College of Arts & Sciences (CAS) while maintaining a global institutional perspective. 2.\tProvide supervision of department chairs in CAS 3.\tActively and persistently foster interdisciplinary cooperation/collaboration across the college and across the University. 4.\tProvide leadership to search and hire full time faculty and to provide a common orientation for adjunct faculty. 5.\tOversee and ensure equitable distribution of faculty loads within CAS. 6.\tOversee departmental annual program review in traditional undergraduate programs 7.\tDevelop and maintain academic policies for the traditional undergraduate program 8.\tProvide Leadership of General Education Committee as ex officio member 9.\tOversee curriculum development, review, revisions for the traditional undergraduate program 10.\tOversee new faculty onboarding 11.\tServe as an active member on Provost Council 12.\tProvide other program oversight and considerations as determined by mutual agreement with Provost 13.\tAssist in providing leadership in meeting goals of university strategic plan 14.\tOversee development and implementation of Winter term courses 15.\tImplement and administer policies and regulations affecting students, including oversight of student requests, complaints, and grievances in academic unit 16.\tProvide direction and oversight in CAS faculty evaluations 17.\tProvide direct support for the Provost in the administration of all academic programs 18.\tAssist Provost in development of academic majors and prioritization 19.\tRepresent the Office of the Provost to external constituents in the provost’s absence 20.\tTeach 1-2 courses per academic year in the dean’s disciplinary area Physical Requirements: Job   Title : Associate   Provost and Dean of Arts & Sciences Typical   Working Conditions: (Describe environment including exposure to heat, cold, fumes, chemicals,   allergens, mold, etc.) Indoors   in controlled environment Equipment   Used: (List all manual and automated equipment used in the course of performing   essential functions.) Computer,   scanner, copier, mouse, keyboard, stapler, 3-hole punch, letter opener Essential   Physical Tasks: (List all physical tasks encountered in performing essential functions - i.e.   sitting for long periods of time using a computer, standing, climbing   ladders, etc.) Sitting   for long periods of time using a computer Analysis of Physical Demands to Perform Essential Functions: Key (Based on typical week): N =Never R =Rarely (Less than 1 hour per week) O =Occasional (1%-33% of time) F =Frequent (34%-66% of time) C =Constant (over 66% of time) Activity Frequency Activity Frequency N R O F C N R O F C Lifting/Carrying Twisting/Turning Under   10 lbs X Reach   over shoulder X 11-20   lbs X Reach   over head X 21-50   lbs X Reach   outward X 51-100   lbs X Climb X Over   100 lbs X Crawl X Kneel X Pushing/Pulling Squat X Under   10 lbs X Sit X 11-20   lbs X Walk-Normal   Surfaces X 21-50   lbs X Walk-Uneven   Surfaces X 51-100   lbs X Walk-Slippery   Surfaces X Over   100 lbs X Stand X Bend X Driving Automatic   Trans X Standard   Trans X Other Keyboard/Ten   Key X Fingering   (fine dexterity) X Handling   (grasping, holding) X Repetitive   Motion – Hands X Repetitive   Motion - Feet X Job Information Job Category: Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Salary: $76,000 - $83,000 Per Year Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Dean for the School of Engineering and Computer Science Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 21, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Chair, Department of Teacher Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Provost and Executive Vice President Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 11, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering (General) Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Science Cedarville University Cedarville, Ohio Posted - September 1, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Pennsylvania Texas California West Palm Beach, Florida Grand Rapids, Michigan Illinois Iowa Charleston, South Carolina Minnesota Ohio Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Wheaton, Illinois Chicago, Illinois Florida South Carolina Houston, Texas ORANGE CITY, Iowa Michigan Redding, California Azusa, California Birmingham, Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota Cedarville, Ohio Alabama Longview, Texas Trending Companies Simpson University Palm Beach Atlantic University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Wheaton College InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Cedarville University Messiah University Calvin University Azusa Pacific University Samford University Charleston Southern University Northwestern College Anderson University - SC Moody Bible Institute Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Business Accounting / Finance Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Executive Faculty Careers - Mathematics Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Hig