    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/director-of-graduate-teacher-education-shawnee-oklahoma-12662": {
      "title": "Director of Graduate Teacher Education",
      "description": "Director of Graduate Teacher Education in Shawnee, Oklahoma (Hybrid) | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Director of Graduate Teacher Education Oklahoma Baptist University Shawnee, Oklahoma (Hybrid) Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 500 W University St, Shawnee, OK 74804, USA OBU Mission Statement OBU transforms lives by equipping students to pursue academic excellence, integrate faith with all areas of knowledge, engage a diverse world, and live worthy of the high calling of God in Christ. Expectations for all Employees Oklahoma Baptist University achieves its mission through a shared commitment to the following expectations. All employees must embrace these expectations and model them in their behavior. Demonstrate      commitment to the essentials of the Christian faith. Commit to the      mission and vision of Oklahoma Baptist University. Treat people with      dignity and respect. Build      relationships on honesty, integrity, and trust. Strive for      excellence through teamwork, leadership, and a strong work ethic. Manage human and      financial resources wisely and efficiently. Purpose : Oklahoma Baptist University seeks a dynamic, mission-driven Administrative Faculty member to serve as the Director of Graduate Teacher Education. This position will provide leadership for graduate education programs in the School of Education, including the Master of Arts in Teaching, the alternative certificate program (ACCESS), and future programs such as a Master of Educational Leadership and Doctorate in Education. The Director will oversee program operations, student support, recruitment, program development, and strategic growth. This role is designed to strengthen support for current and prospective graduate students while advancing the School of Education’s online, nontraditional, and graduate offerings. The position includes both teaching and administrative responsibilities, with an anticipated 50/50 split that includes approximately six credit hours of teaching per semester. The Director will report to the Dean for Online, Nontraditional, and Graduate Education, serve as a faculty member in the School of Education, and work with the Director for Teacher Education on curricular oversight related to specialized accreditation. The Teacher Education program at OBU is accredited by the Council for the Accreditation of Education Preparation (CAEP) and by the Office of Education Quality and Accountability (OEQA). Essential Functions: Graduate Program Leadership and Operations Provide      leadership for graduate teacher education programs, including the Master      of Arts in Teaching and ACCESS programs. Oversee      day-to-day operations for the MAT and ACCESS programs. Collaborate      with School of Education faculty and leadership to ensure graduate      programs reflect institutional mission, program goals, and professional      standards. Coordinate      onboarding and advising for new MAT and ACCESS students. Serve      as a primary point of contact for current and prospective graduate teacher      education students. Answer      prospective student questions and provide timely communication regarding      program requirements, admission pathways, course sequencing, and licensure      expectations. Collaborate      with faculty, staff, and administrators to ensure quality and consistency      in graduate program delivery. Assist      with scheduling, course planning, staffing needs, and communication      specific to graduate education programs. Maintain      accurate records and documentation related to advising, student progress,      and program operations. Support      coordination between graduate programs and relevant undergraduate or      integrated pathways, including students pursuing integrated MAT options. Program Development and Strategic Growth Provide      leadership for the future development of graduate education offerings,      including potential programs such as a Master of Educational Leadership      and Doctorate in Education within the School of Education. Collaborate      with School of Education and graduate administrative leadership to      identify opportunities for program expansion and innovation. Support      efforts to develop graduate programs that respond to the needs of schools,      districts, adult learners, and education professionals. Develop      and oversee a Graduate Teacher Education Program Handbook. Contribute      to strategic planning related to graduate teacher education enrollment,      partnerships, and long-term program growth. Assist      in developing pathways that connect undergraduate teacher education      students, integrated MAT students, school partners, and other prospective      students to graduate education opportunities. Teaching Responsibilities Teach      approximately six credit hours per semester in graduate or teacher      education programs. Ensure      courses reflect best practices in online pedagogy, graduate education, and      teacher preparation. Provide      timely feedback, meaningful engagement, and academic support to students. Contribute      to course development, revision, and continuous improvement in alignment      with university expectations and accreditation standards. Model      effective teaching practices for online, adult, nontraditional, and      graduate learners. Recruitment, Partnerships, and External Engagement Plan,      assist with, and participate in recruitment events for graduate teacher      education programs, including grant writing for such events. Support      major recruitment initiatives such as Crash Course in Teaching, a summer      Teacher Literacy Academy, ACSI events, RestorEd, Avedis Celebrate      Educators events, school partnership events, and other relevant      opportunities. Collaborate      with Marketing and Communications, Admissions, and Advancement by      providing program input when requested. Help      develop clear and compelling communication about graduate education      programs for prospective students and external partners. Collaborate      with the admissions office and other relevant campus offices and personnel      for recruitment and retention of new students and school partnerships. Represent      graduate teacher education programs professionally in internal and      external settings. Collaborate      with stakeholders and partners to construct mutually beneficial P-12      school and community arrangements for clinical and candidate preparation. Accreditation & Assessment <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>Serve on the Teacher Education Committee, representing advanced programs. Oversee      accreditation efforts for advanced graduate education programs in      collaboration with the Executive Director for Teacher Education, Director      of Teacher Education Assessment & Accreditation, faculty, and other      university personnel. Support      specialized accreditation processes related to advanced programs,      including CAEP, OEQA, SPAs, state licensure requirements, and other      relevant standards. Contribute      to assessment, data collection, reporting, and continuous improvement      processes to maintain a quality assurance system for graduate education      programs. Ensure      graduate teacher education programs remain aligned with institutional,      state, accreditation, and licensure expectations. Use      data-informed decision-making and stakeholder feedback to improve student      success, program quality, and program outcomes. Collaboration and Institutional Service Participate      in the Council for Online, Nontraditional, and Graduate Education      Programs. Collaborate      regularly with the Dean for Online, Nontraditional, and Graduate      Education. Work      closely with the Director for Teacher Education on curricular matters      related to specialized accreditation. Serve      as a faculty member within the School of Education and participate in      faculty meetings, committees, and initiatives as appropriate. Collaborate      with faculty, admissions staff, marketing personnel, advancement staff,      school partners, and other stakeholders to support graduate education      programs. Participate      in campus faculty development opportunities. Contribute      to university and School of Education committee work and initiatives as      assigned. Other Duties: Remain      professionally active through appropriate conferences, professional      organizations, presentations, scholarship, or service. Stay      current on trends in teacher education, graduate education, online      learning, school partnerships, and educator preparation. Perform      other duties as assigned in support of the mission of the university and      the School of Education. Required Qualifications: Must      hold a current teaching and administrative license or relevant      education-related licensure. Experience      in teacher education, PK–12 education, graduate education, online      education, or a related field. Demonstrated      ability to teach in higher education or professional education settings. Strong      organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Student-centered      mindset with a commitment to graduate student success, retention, and      completion. Ability      to manage multiple priorities, programs, deadlines, and stakeholder      relationships. Strong      problem-solving and data-informed decision-making skills. Effective      use of technology in online teaching, communication, and program      management. Commitment      to the mission of Oklahoma Baptist University. Education: <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]> Required: Doctorate in Education or a related field, or active progress toward completion of a terminal degree. Preferred: Experience: Required: <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>Must hold a current teaching and administrative license or relevant education-related licensure. Experience      in teacher education, PK–12 education, graduate education, or a related      field. Preferred: Current      principal and/or superintendent license or relevant education-related      licensure. Experience      in public and/or private school administration. Experience      teaching in online, hybrid, graduate, or adult-learning formats. Experience      with graduate program leadership, program development, or academic      administration. Experience      with alternative certification or nontraditional teacher preparation pathways. Experience      with CAEP, OEQA, state licensure requirements, and/or advanced program      accreditation. Experience      developing or leading master’s or doctoral programs in education. Experience      supporting diverse, adult, online, or nontraditional student populations. Experience      with recruitment, school partnerships, and educator pipeline development. Physical Requirements: <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>This will be a 12-month faculty appointment. <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>The position may be eligible for remote or hybrid work, depending on institutional needs. <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>Occasional travel or on-campus presence may be required for meetings, trainings, or events. Special Requirements: <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>Must be a member of a local evangelical* Christian church. *Evangelical is a broad term referring to segment within Christianity which maintains the authority of the Bible and the belief in salvation by faith in Jesus alone. <![if !supportLists]> · <![endif]>Please apply using the link for “Faculty Applications” on the OBU website at: https://www.okbu.edu/hr/jobs.html OBU Benefits Summary: OBU understands that our employees are our most valuable assets when fulfilling our mission. We strive to offer an extensive array of benefits and opportunities for employees to choose from. Full-time employees benefit from the generous OBU provision of premium contributions for nationwide family-friendly Health and Dental coverages along with free life insurance that includes accidental death and dismemberment equal to an employee’s base salary. OBU provides access to optional employee-paid ancillary benefits like vision, hospitalization, critical illness, accident, additional employee-paid family life insurance coverages, and education benefits at OBU and other institutions of higher education. There is generous paid time off that includes annual granted vacation time, accrued sick leave, six annual holidays, and week-long breaks for Thanksgiving and Christmas that include energy conservation days. For all employees working at least half-time, there is an employer matching opportunity for retirement investments in a 403(b)(9) plan administered by Guide Stone. There are numerous other perks and opportunities for OBU employees including FREE family membership to the OBU Recreation and Wellness Center or RAWC, Global outreach university mission trips, cafeteria discounts, and parking privileges to name a few. For more information about the current OBU employee benefits and opportunities, please contact the Human Resources staff at [email protected] . Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Education Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Director, MA in Counseling Program Geneva College Beaver Falls, Pennsylvania Posted - September 22, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Open Rank Faculty Position, Tech and Human Flourishing LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Azusa, California Alabama Minnesota Texas Houston, Texas Wheaton, Illinois California Grand Rapids, Michigan Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Charleston, South Carolina Cedarville, Ohio Redding, California Florida Birmingham, Alabama Illinois St. Paul, Minnesota ORANGE CITY, Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Iowa Longview, Texas South Carolina Chicago, Illinois Pennsylvania Michigan Ohio Trending Companies Samford University Simpson University Messiah University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Anderson University - SC Calvin University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Wheaton College Moody Bible Institute Charleston Southern University Azusa Pacific University Northwestern College Cedarville University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Education Executive Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Business Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
