    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-accounting-longview-texas-12567": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA POSITION DESCRIPTION : LeTourneau University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in accounting beginning Spring or Fall of 2027. Successful candidates will demonstrate subject matter expertise in the field of accounting and other related business disciplines. The candidate will be expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels in both online and in-person modalities. The candidate will show evidence of teaching excellence, skill in engaging students through active and collaborative learning, competent use of instructional technology, exceptional oral and written communication skills, and a demonstrated scholarship potential. LeTourneau seeks candidates who are excited about collaborating with existing faculty and other stakeholders to expand an innovative and regionally engaged business program. QUALIFICATIONS: An enthusiastic and contagious Christian faith and a commitment to Christian higher education that integrates Christian faith and learning Authentic support and enthusiasm for the university’s statement of faith and community covenant Preferred qualifications include a CPA and a Ph.D. or DBA in Accounting; candidates with a Master’s Degree in Accountancy, a CPA, and substantial industry experience will also be considered An ability to lead students in hands-on learning with a special emphasis on the latest innovations and technologies impacting their area of expertise; evidence of successful university-level teaching is highly desirable Excellent interpersonal skills; team-oriented approach to tasks; and willingness to contribute to all the programs within the School of Business A demonstrated commitment to ongoing professional engagement and scholarly activity commensurate with academic rank SALARY AND BENEFITS: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. PROCEDURE FOR APPLICATION OR NOMINATION: Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. The review process will begin as early as October 1st, 2026, and all applications received by October 15th, 2026, will receive full consideration. Applications after that date will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty . Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . ABOUT LETOURNEAU UNIVERSITY : LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Commission on Colleges and Universities and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. LeTourneau is consistently recognized by U.S. News and World Report as one of \"America's Best Colleges.\" The School of Business, accredited through the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP), prepares students for the workplace through hands-on learning in real-world applications, resulting in a ninety-nine percent graduate job placement rate. LeTourneau ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information.  Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Business Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View School of Business Marketing Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Spring Arbor University Spring Arbor, Michigan Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Wheaton, Illinois Texas Longview, Texas Florida Cedarville, Ohio Birmingham, Alabama Alabama Azusa, California ORANGE CITY, Iowa West Palm Beach, Florida Houston, Texas South Carolina Minnesota Anderson, South Carolina Illinois Pennsylvania Iowa Michigan Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Grand Rapids, Michigan California Redding, California Ohio St. Paul, Minnesota Chicago, Illinois Charleston, South Carolina Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Messiah University Wheaton College Azusa Pacific University Moody Bible Institute Samford University Cedarville University Northwestern College Anderson University - SC Simpson University LeTourneau University Calvin University Houston Christian University Charleston Southern University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Psychology Executive Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Other Education NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Engineering Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
