    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/director-the-center-for-academic-ministry-longview-texas-12565": {
      "title": "Director, The Center for Academic MInistry",
      "description": "Director, The Center for Academic MInistry in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA Title: Director, The Center for Academic Ministry (CAM) Reports to: Dean, School of Theology and Vocation Position Type: Tenure-track faculty; 11-month contract Teaching load: 1-1-1 per AY Location: Longview, TX LeTourneau University invites applications for the Director of the Center for Academic Ministry (CAM), an 11-month, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor. The Center for Academic Ministry exists to empower faculty and staff to shepherd students in faith integration and spiritual formation for the sake of the church and the world. Backed by a significant endowment, this center supports the university’s mission of nurturing Christian virtue and cultivating faith integration that impacts all areas of students’ lives. While the position reports within the School of Theology and Vocation, the candidate’s primary discipline and terminal degree may be within any academic field represented at LeTourneau University. The Director is responsible for developing, implementing, and strategically leading programs that foster faith integration and spiritual formation across the academic and co-curricular life of the institution. This role collaborates closely with faculty, staff, academic schools, and campus partners to cultivate a robust culture of faithful and reflective academic ministry that is grounded in LeTourneau’s Theology and Vocation Core curriculum, pedagogical excellence, and holistic care for students. Key Responsibilities Lead faculty development and faith-integration      training programs Facilitate seminars, reading groups, and      interdisciplinary learning communities Direct the Koinonia Institute faculty and staff      retreats Assess and strengthen faith-integration efforts      across academic and student-facing programs Develop certificate and credentialing      opportunities in academic ministry Oversee CAM communications, digital resources, and      website content Foster mentorship networks and learning communities      for faculty and staff Manage CAM strategic planning, budgeting,      partnerships, and institutional engagement Required Qualifications Terminal degree in a relevant field; formal      theological education preferred Demonstrated experience in faith integration,      Christian higher education, and academic ministry Strong teaching, facilitation, and communication      skills Experience designing and leading faculty      development and/or spiritual formation programs Ability to assess program effectiveness and communicate      results effectively Preferred Qualifications Experience in Christian higher education      leadership or academic administration Scholarly engagement in faith integration, Christian      theology, vocation, pedagogy, or related themes Experience directing retreats or spiritual      formation initiatives Familiarity with web content management and      digital resource development Personal Characteristics Consistent evidence of spiritual growth and faith      integration Collaborative leadership style with the ability to      inspire and mobilize diverse campus constituents Strategic thinker capable of envisioning and      building sustainable programs Pastoral sensitivity and a heart for shepherding      educators in their vocation of academic ministry Salary and Benefits Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University offers group health insurance plans, life insurance, contribution to a retirement program, and undergraduate tuition waivers for employees and their dependents, among other benefits. Date Position is Available : Spring or Fall 2027 Procedure for Application or Nomination Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form at the link below. The review process will begin as early as October 1st, 2026, and all applications received by October 15th, 2026, will receive full consideration. Applications after that date will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty . Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . About the University LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information. Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Other Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Facu