    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-nursing-la-mirada-california-12666": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing in La Mirada, California | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Biola University La Mirada, California Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 13800 Biola Ave, La Mirada, CA 90639, USA Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing The Department of Nursing at Biola University is now accepting applications for an Assistant/Associate tenure-track full-time faculty position to begin in August 2027. Responsibilities: Provide instruction in the following clinical/theory areas- Nursing leadership,  Healthcare Management, and DNP courses including support with project development, and pathophysiology. Provide feedback to students via online learning activities and assessment of assignments submitted through the Learning Management System (i.e., Canvas). Demonstrate excellent communication, accountability, and initiative, along with a strong Christian commitment and interest in the integration of faith with learning. Provide academic advising and mentoring for students towards a future career and in their Christian faith. Remain current in their field by engaging in scholarly or clinical work and being active in professional organizations. Participate in course, curriculum, and program development. Work strategically with diverse colleagues, students, and community members. Participate in campus, university, and community service activities. Qualifications: A doctoral degree (PhD or DNP) in nursing that includes clinical preparation in a nursing specialty and preparation for the teaching role is required. Demonstrated expertise in a nursing specialty area. Two years of clinical experience in the area of instruction and a minimum of one year full-time equivalency in clinical practice preferred. Current California RN license Current CPR Healthcare Provider Card at time of hire. Possess a commitment to high-quality instruction in an in-person or online student-centered environment. Proficient in computer, online, and learning management system skills. The School of Science, Technology, and Health (SSTH) at Biola University serves both graduate and undergraduate students. The undergraduate program of the SSTH is the largest among the seven schools that comprise Biola University. Our mission is to train professionals who are grounded in a Christian worldview, are intellectually and technically proficient and are prepared to provide clear moral leadership in their respective fields. Our school is committed to a biblical vision of unity where diverse believers work together as one body under the lordship of Christ. Candidates from diverse backgrounds, cultures and experiences are encouraged to apply. Biola is an evangelical Christian university in which faculty endorse a university statement of Christian faith and community values, and are committed to the integration of faith and learning.  Candidates must be willing to support Biola’s mission, and preference will be given to applicants who demonstrate a clear commitment to the integration of faith into their scholarship and teaching. Biola serves a student body of over 5,500 undergraduate and graduate students and is accredited by WASC. As a private Christian University, Biola seeks faculty whose personal theological beliefs are in agreement with the Biola Theological Positions and maintain a lifestyle consistent with the Biola Standard of Conduct. Applicants should send their CV, one-page statement of interest, and one-page Christian testimony through this online system ( https://www.biola.edu/hr/employment ) . Review of applications will start immediately until the position is filled. If you have questions about items for the application, please contact Fay Jaime Executive Assistant/ Director of Operations at [email protected] . Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Health Professions Salary: $83,688 - $109,330 Per Year Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Visiting Professor-Biology Southern Nazarene University Bethany, Oklahoma Posted - September 25, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Communication LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Education LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Construction Management LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 15, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Michigan Upland, Indiana Georgia California Cedarville, Ohio Chicago, Illinois Azusa, California Minnesota Indiana Pennsylvania Longview, Texas Grand Rapids, Michigan South Carolina West Palm Beach, Florida Florida Birmingham, Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania ORANGE CITY, Iowa Ohio Alabama Redding, California Lookout Mountain, Georgia Houston, Texas Charleston, South Carolina Illinois Iowa Wheaton, Illinois Texas Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Calvin University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Northwestern College Samford University LeTourneau University Simpson University Palm Beach Atlantic University Moody Bible Institute Cedarville University Anderson University - SC Houston Christian University Covenant College Messiah University Charleston Southern University Taylor University Wheaton College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Car