    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-faculty-position-in-poverty-and-development-lookout-mountain-georgia-12693": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development in Lookout Mountain, Georgia | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure Track Faculty Position in Poverty and Development Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Share Save Job Apply for This Job The Department of Economics and Development at Covenant College, an agency of the Presbyterian Church in America and an academically rigorous Christian college emphasizing the liberal arts in the Reformed and Presbyterian tradition, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position beginning July 1, 2027. Rank and compensation will be commensurate with experience. While remaining firmly committed to its foundational commitments with respect to poverty alleviation, the college has adopted a new Poverty and Development Program, which equips students to seek creative solutions to poverty in a much wider range of settings and sectors than ever before. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach a variety of undergraduate courses related to poverty and development that reflect both the current needs of the department and the professor’s particular areas of expertise and interest. Teach multiple sections of a junior-level core curriculum course focused on faithful engagement with issues related to poverty and migration. Work with partner organizations to create outstanding, summer-long field experiences for undergraduate students Engage in research, scholarship, and other professional activities Mentor and advise undergraduate students Participate in the life of the campus community and faculty governance Qualifications: Ph.D. in Community Development, Intercultural Studies, Public Administration, or related field from a regionally accredited institution by July 1, 2027 preferred. Candidates with Master's Degrees will also be considered. Field experience in facilitation, program design, or evaluation in a range of cross-cultural settings Demonstrated excellence in teaching Enthusiasm for working with undergraduates in applied, cross-cultural research Commitment to the mission of Covenant College Interested and qualified candidates should send the following documentation to Dr. Collin Messer: Letter of Interest indicating teaching and research interests Curriculum Vitae A Testimony of Christian Faith and Experience Philosophy of Christian Higher Education A Response to the Westminster Confession (located at https://www.pcaac.org/bco/westminster-confession/ indicating agreement, and any scruples, with rationales, with the Confession Dr. Collin Messer Vice-President for Academic Affairs Covenant College 14049 Scenic Highway Lookout Mountain, GA 30750 Email: [email protected] Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Other Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Tenure Track Faculty Position in Christian Ministry Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View Tenure Track Faculty Position in Finance Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Posted - September 24, 2026 View FACULTY POSITION in Department of Sports Medicine & Exercise Science Belhaven University Jackson, Mississippi Posted - September 10, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Applied Health Sciences Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Biblical Studies Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Psychology Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Indiana Upland, Indiana South Carolina Azusa, California Wheaton, Illinois Alabama Redding, California Charleston, South Carolina Oh