    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-faculty-position-in-ecology-environmental-biology-lookout-mountain-georgia-12692": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology in Lookout Mountain, Georgia | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure Track Faculty Position in Ecology/Environmental Biology Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Share Save Job Apply for This Job The Department of Biology at Covenant College, an agency of the Presbyterian Church in America and an academically rigorous Christian college emphasizing the liberal arts in the Reformed and Presbyterian tradition, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position beginning July 1, 2027. Rank and compensation will be commensurate with experience. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach a sophomore-level Ecology course, upper-level elective courses in ecology or environmental biology, and a lab science course for non-majors Maintain and strengthen our existing consortial partnership with the Au Sable Institute of Environmental Studies, and to oversee Covenant’s environmental stewardship and sustainability certificate program. Engage in research, scholarship, and other professional activities Mentor and advise undergraduate students Participate in the life of the campus community and faculty governance Qualifications: A doctoral degree with specialization in ecology or environmental biology is required. Preference will be given to those candidates with teaching experience and interest in establishing an active field of research program with undergraduates that can take advantage of Covenant’s land holding and location in southern Appalachia. Demonstrated excellence in teaching and research Commitment to the mission of Covenant College Interested and qualified candidates should send the following documentation to Dr. Collin Messer at [email protected] : Curriculum Vitae A Testimony of Christian Faith and Experience Philosophy of Christian Higher Education A Response to the Westminster Confession (located at https://www.pcaac.org/bco/westminster-confession/ indicating agreement, and any scruples, with rationales Dr. Collin Messer Vice-President for Academic Affairs Covenant College 14049 Scenic Highway Lookout Mt., GA 30750 Email: [email protected] Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Biology/ Life Sciences Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Jim and Sharon Harrod Chair of Christian Thought & Full-Time Tenure Track Position Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - September 17, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor in Healthcare Management and Leadership Montreat College Montreat, North Carolina Posted - September 16, 2026 View Assistant/ Associate Professor of Biology or Kinesiology Simpson University Redding, California Posted - September 15, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Biology Charleston Southern University Charleston, South Carolina Posted - September 10, 2026 View Biology Faculty Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Posted - September 2, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Applied Health Sciences Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Assistant Professor Of Marketing Campus Ministry Director Trending Locations Redding, California St. Paul, Minnesota Wheaton, Illinois Indiana Pennsylvania Alabama Longview, Texas Illinois Georgia Charleston, South Carolina West Palm Beach, Florida Ohio Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Chicago, Illinois South Carolina California Lookout Mountain, Georgia Iowa Houston, Texas Minnesota Grand Rapids, Michigan Birmingham, Alabama Michigan Azusa, California Upland, Indiana Texas ORANGE CITY, Iowa Cedarville, Ohio Florida Trending Companies Simpson University Palm Beach Atlantic University Northwestern College Houston Christian University Charleston Southern University LeTourneau University Anderson