      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing in Lookout Mountain, Georgia | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure Track Faculty Position in English/Writing Covenant College Lookout Mountain, Georgia Share Save Job Apply for This Job The English Department at Covenant College, an agency of the Presbyterian Church in America and an academically rigorous Christian college emphasizing the liberal arts in the Reformed and Presbyterian tradition, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position beginning July 1, 2027. Rank and compensation will be commensurate with experience. The English Department at Covenant College is seeking someone with a degree in writing and the experience and expertise to teach a variety of courses in the department’s writing concentration. In addition to teaching English Composition and Introduction to Creative Writing, the ideal candidate will also be able to direct a writing center and/or teach two or more of the following courses: Journalism, Introduction to Professional Writing, Fiction, Poetry, Creative Nonfiction. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach 2-3 writing courses each semester Teach 1-2 core courses each semester Advise and mentor students Meet with prospective students Supervise the student newspaper and/or the student literary magazine Participate in the life of the campus community and faculty governance Qualifications: A terminal degree (MFA or PhD) in writing from a regionally accredited institution Demonstrated excellence in teaching Interest in mentoring undergraduates Commitment to the mission of Covenant College Interested and qualified candidates should email the following documentation to Dr. Collin Messer, Vice President for Academic Affairs, Covenant College, at [email protected] : Letter of Interest indicating 