    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-in-elementary-education-upland-indiana-12686": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track in Elementary Education",
      "description": "Tenure-Track in Elementary Education in Upland, Indiana | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure-Track in Elementary Education Taylor University Upland, Indiana Share Save Job Apply for This Job Taylor University is seeking applications and nominations of distinguished candidates for a tenure-track faculty position in Education beginning in August 20 2 7 . R ank and salary are dependent upon qualifications and experience . Mission and Commitment Taylor's mission is to develop servant-leaders marked with a passion to minister Christ’s redemptive love, grace, and truth to a world in need. As a community, Taylor faculty, staff, and students commit to living out Christ’s love and truth in the here and now. We worship together, serve one another, and grow in faith as we learn in the classroom, on the field, at chapel, and anywhere else we’re doing Life Together. Duties and Responsibilities Teach a full-timeload of 24-load hours per academic year for undergraduate courses in elementary education, with a primary emphasis on early childhood and elementary literacy instruction. Design interactive and engaging classroom experiences that integrate faith into the curriculum and model evidence-based practices in early literacy, including the development of foundational reading and writing skills and effective instruction for diverse learners. Advise students on licensure requirements, degree progress, and professional development while coaching students in the professional and ethical practices expected of elementary educators. Supervise and mentor pre-service teachers through advising, field experiences, and student teaching. Collaborate with Education Department colleagues to strengthen the elementary education program including contributions to accreditation reports and ensure alignment with state and national standards for educator preparation. Serve the university, community, and profession through committee work, partnerships with local schools, participation in faculty governance, and involvement in relevant professional organizations. Participate in professional development and continuing education to remain current with research, policy, and emerging practices in elementary education, early childhood literacy, and reading instruction. Conduct scholarly research and/or engage in scholarly activity that contributes to the fields of elementary education, literacy education, teacher preparation, or related areas. Possess excellent interpersonal, oral, written communication, and organizational skills. Attend chapel and participate in the broader spiritual and community life of the university. Typical Qualifications Candidates must have a personal, vibrant faith and Christian walk and be strongly committed to the educational mission and evangelical Christian orientation of the University. Taylor University is a Christ-centered educational institution, and an evangelical, interdenominational covenant community committed to advancing life-long learning and ministering the redemptive love and truth of Jesus Christ to a world in need. Candidates will be expected to affirm the Taylor University Life Together Covenant, Statement of Faith, and essential documents. An earned doctorate in education or a related field is preferred. ABD and master’s-level candidates may be considered. Evidence of significant effective instructional experience and a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching is essential. The candidate should have diverse teaching experiences and expertise in elementary education methods, with demonstrated knowledge of and experience with evidence-based literacy instruction aligned with the Science of Reading. Experience teaching early childhood literacy is preferred. The successful candidate will contribute to our dynamic teacher preparation program by preparing future elementary educators who are competent, caring, reflective, and prepared for world service. Supplemental Information The Education Department comprises eleven faculty and staff and is accredited by CAEP and the Indiana Department of Education. Undergraduate Teacher Education candidates may obtain licensure in All-grade (P-12) Art and Music Education, K-6 Elementary Education, and Secondary Education (grades 5-12) offered in Biology, Chemistry, English, English/Theatre Arts, Mathematics, Mathematics/Computer Science, Physics, Physics/Mathematics, Physical Science, Social Studies and Spanish. Additional licensure offerings include Mild and Intense Intervention and Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages. The Taylor University Education Department also offers Transition to Teaching and Online Licensure Programs ( https://www.taylor.edu/online/programs-licensures/transition-to-teaching ). Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Education Related Jobs Top Private Elementary Christian School in Seoul, S. Korea Young Hoon Elementary Christian School Seoul, Korea, South Posted - August 26, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Applied Health Sciences Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Biblical Studies Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Psychology Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Full-Time Mechanical, or Biomedical Engineering, or Engineering Physics Faculty Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Full-time Faculty in Biology Messiah University Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Posted - September 25, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Campus Ministry Director Assistant Professor Of Marketing Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Lookout Mountain, Georgia Upland, Indiana South Carolina Azusa, California ORANGE CITY, Iowa Houston, Texas Iowa Minnesota St. Paul, Minnesota Redding, California Alabama Charleston, South Carolina Wheaton, Illinois West Palm Beach, Florida Illinois Chicago, Illinois Michigan Longview, Texas Georgia Birmingham, Alabama Florida California Pennsylvania Grand Rapids, Michigan Indiana Ohio Cedarville, Ohio Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania Texas Trending Companies Simpson University InterVarsity Christian Fellowship/USA Samford University Cedarville University Anderson University - SC Messiah University Houston Christian University Covenant College Taylor University Wheaton College Azusa Pacific University Calvin University Northwestern College LeTourneau University Moody Bible Institute Palm Beach Atlantic University Charleston Southern University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Mathematics Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Executive Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar NonProfit Careers Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Accounting / Finance Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Education Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Accounting / Finance Education Executive Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences NonProfit Careers Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Deans Faculty Careers - Business Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Admissions/Registrar Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Mathematics Faculty Careers - Fine and Performing Arts Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
